//! Generated in-source native call contract reference.
//!
//! Registration/ABI, candidate naming, target recovery, and Rust implementation
//! are deliberately reported as separate facts. A third-party name or a Rust
//! match arm does not make a handler target-confirmed.
//! Arguments are listed in BP push order; native handlers pop them from the end.
//!
//! ## System group 0x80
//!
//! `0x80:0x00` `Sys80_00_Srand`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[seed: u32 seed]. Target handler 0x00487D20 pops one DWORD and calls the imported Microsoft CRT srand directly.
//! `0x80:0x01` `Sys80_01_Rand`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[none]. Target handler 0x00487D40 calls the imported rand and pushes its result unchanged.
//! `0x80:0x02` `Sys80_02_RandMax`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[max_exclusive: i32]. Target handler 0x00487D60 combines three CRT rand calls as (((r0<<8)^r1)<<8)^r2 before signed remainder by a positive bound.
//! `0x80:0x04` `Sys80_04_GetEngineTick`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[none]. Target 0x00487DB0 calls sub_498720, the pause-adjusted GetTickCount/timeGetTime engine clock.
//! `0x80:0x05` `Sys80_05_QueryPerformanceCounterNs`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[counter_out: BP pointer to u64]. Target 0x00487DD0 writes a u64 equal to counter/frequency*1,000,000,000; failed Win32 queries fall back to the engine millisecond clock and frequency 1000.
//! `0x80:0x06` `Sys80_06_SetPerformanceProfiling`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[enabled: bool/i32]. Target 0x00487E00 writes dword_565AC4 and, when enabled, resets accumulated count, time, dispersion and frame budget state.
//! `0x80:0x07` `Sys80_07_ReadPerformanceMetric`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[output_ptr: BP pointer to i32; metric_id: i32 enum 0..=3]. Target 0x00487E20 calls sub_401670. Selector 0 returns sample count; 1 average microseconds; 2 a 1/10000 throughput ratio; 3 a 1/10000 squared-dispersion ratio.
//! `0x80:0x08` `Sys80_08_ReadCursorPoint`: inputs=0, outputs=2, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[none]. Target 0x00487E50 calls sub_48E680, which prefers captured coordinates and otherwise converts the Win32 cursor position through the active display-mode transform.
//! `0x80:0x09` `Sys80_09_QueryPresentationState`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[none]. Target 0x00487E90 returns dword_565EC4. The render-present path updates it from the engine clock after a successful native present.
//! `0x80:0x0A` `Sys80_0A_CopyGraphicsCapabilities`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: BP pointer to 64-byte record]. Target 0x00487EB0 copies exactly 0x40 bytes from dword_518920, the graphics initialization/capability cache.
//! `0x80:0x0B` `Sys80_0B_QueryGraphicsMemoryMetric`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[none]. Target 0x00487EE0 reaches sub_431130 and returns the DWORD at the active renderer object offset +0x58.
//! `0x80:0x0C` `Sys80_0C_GetLocalTime`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: BP pointer to SYSTEMTIME]. Target 0x00487F00 passes the BP destination directly to Win32 GetLocalTime.
//! `0x80:0x0D` `Sys80_0D_GetPhysicalMemory`: inputs=0, outputs=2, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[none]. Target 0x00487F20 calls GlobalMemoryStatus and clamps each physical-memory value independently to INT32_MAX before pushing it.
//! `0x80:0x0E` `Sys80_0E_QueryWindowMinimizeLatch`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[none]. Target 0x00487FB0 returns dword_5666F4. CloseWindow sets it; WM_ACTIVATE clears it after restoration when the window is no longer iconic.
//! `0x80:0x0F` `Sys80_0F_QueryWindowActive`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[none]. Target 0x00487FD0 returns dword_5666E8, written from WM_ACTIVATE and WM_NCACTIVATE processing.
//! `0x80:0x10` `Sys80_10_ResetInputConfiguration`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[enabled: bool/i32]. Target 0x00487FF0 stores dword_506A44 through sub_46D970, then sub_46DA20 clears every six-DWORD input-state record.
//! `0x80:0x11` `Sys80_11_QueryKeyDown`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[descriptor: i32 target logical input descriptor]. Target 0x00488010 calls sub_46D560 and returns bit 15. The helper applies logical mouse-button swapping and active-window gating before GetAsyncKeyState.
//! `0x80:0x12` `Sys80_12_SumInputDescriptorState`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[descriptors: pointer to linked/zero-terminated descriptor record]. Target 0x00488040 traverses a descriptor chain and sums dword_518CA4[6*descriptor] through sub_46DC70.
//! `0x80:0x13` `Sys80_13_GetInputMessageSerial`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[none]. Target-confirmed: handler 0x00488080 calls sub_46E5C0, which returns dword_56683C. sub_46E5B0 increments that global from the window/input message path.
//! `0x80:0x14` `Sys80_14_SetInputMasterGate`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[value: i32 configuration value]. Target-confirmed: handler 0x004880A0 pops one i32 and writes dword_506A48 through sub_46D980.
//! `0x80:0x15` `Sys80_15_SetInputLatchedState`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[value: i32 configuration value]. Target-confirmed: handler 0x004880C0 pops one i32 and writes dword_566828 through sub_46D990.
//! `0x80:0x16` `Sys80_16_SampleConfiguredInput`: inputs=0, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[none]. Target-confirmed: handler 0x004880E0 calls sub_46D9A0, arms the one-shot configured-input poll flag and samples every registered descriptor without writing a BP result.
//! `0x80:0x17` `Sys80_17_QueryConfiguredInputGate`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[none]. Target-confirmed: handler 0x004880F0 returns sub_46DE30, which combines the active-window state, both configuration globals and sampled key/input state.
//! `0x80:0x18` `Sys80_18_RegisterInputScope`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[scope: i32 input scope]. Target-confirmed: handler 0x00488110 registers the packed scope through sub_46D6C0 and sub_46D720, then performs one stateful sub_46DF00 query. Only its return is discarded; the query drains event count and first-held latch state.
//! `0x80:0x19` `Sys80_19_QueryAndUnregisterInputScope`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[scope: i32 input scope]. Target-confirmed: handler 0x00488150 queries the packed scope and removes it from both target lists through sub_46D7A0/sub_46D7B0.
//! `0x80:0x1A` `Sys80_1A_QueryInputEventBits`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[scope: i32 registration scope]. Reports real input events only. Input configuration registers must not synthesize a non-zero result.
//! `0x80:0x1B` `Sys80_1B_RegisterInputClassDescriptors`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[class_mask: i32 target input-class bit; descriptors: pointer to zero-terminated i32 array]. Target-confirmed: handler 0x004881C0 passes the class mask and a zero-terminated descriptor array to sub_46DFA0. The target rejects unknown masks and lists with 16 or more nonzero entries.
//! `0x80:0x1C` `Sys80_1C_QueryInputClassLevel`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[class_mask: i32 input-class mask]. Level query is independent from the edge-triggered event bitmap returned by Sys80_1A.
//! `0x80:0x1D` `Sys80_1D_QueryScopedInputEvent`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[input_descriptor: i32 target logical input descriptor; scope: i32 registration scope]. Target handler 0x00488290 packs scope as (scope << 16) | 0xFFFF, validates descriptors 1/2 through sub_46D830 and all others through sub_46D810, then drains sub_46DB40(input_descriptor).
//! `0x80:0x1E` `Sys80_1E_SetMouseButtonMappingMode`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[mode: i32 enum 0..=1]. Target 0x004882F0 calls sub_48EE50. Only modes 0 and 1 are stored; sub_46D560 uses mode 1 to swap logical descriptors 1 and 2.
//! `0x80:0x1F` `Sys80_1F_ConfigureCursorMotion`: inputs=6, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[cancel_on_large_move: bool/i32; updates_per_second: u32; duration_ms: u32 milliseconds; interpolation_mode: i32 enum; target_y: i32 logical pixels; target_x: i32 logical pixels]. Target handler 0x00488320 forwards six native pops to sub_48E780. The helper captures the current cursor, derives max(updates_per_second * duration_ms / 1000, 1) steps, and advances a linear or cosine interpolation from the per-frame sub_48E930 tick.
//! `0x80:0x20` `Sys80_20_Alloc`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[size: u32 byte count]. Target 0x00488380 validates the requested size, allocates through sub_48DC70's memory-class table and raises the native VM error path when allocation returns zero.
//! `0x80:0x21` `Sys80_21_Free`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[pointer: opaque BP memory pointer]. Target 0x004883D0 treats null as success; non-null handles are decoded by sub_48DD10 and invalid/double-free values enter the native VM error path.
//! `0x80:0x24` `Sys80_24_CountFiles`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[pattern: Shift-JIS path pattern; recursive: bool/i32]. Target 0x00488450 calls sub_466BB0 with no output buffer, unlimited count and the caller's recursive flag.
//! `0x80:0x25` `Sys80_25_EnumerateFiles`: inputs=5, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: BP byte-buffer pointer or null; capacity: i32 byte count; pattern: Shift-JIS path pattern; recursive: bool/i32; max_count: u32]. Target 0x00488490/sub_466BB0 emits packed NUL-terminated names, skips directories in the primary pass and optionally recurses.
//! `0x80:0x26` `Sys80_26_EnumerateDirectories`: inputs=4, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: BP byte-buffer pointer or null; capacity: u32 byte count; pattern: Shift-JIS path pattern; max_count: u32]. Target 0x00488510/sub_466F00 enumerates immediate directories, excluding dot and dot-dot.
//! `0x80:0x27` `Sys80_27_MoveFile`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: Shift-JIS path; source: Shift-JIS path]. Target 0x00488560 calls MoveFileA(first native pop, second native pop), which corresponds to the target's destination-first BP argument order documented here.
//! `0x80:0x28` `Sys80_28_CreateDirectory`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[path: Shift-JIS path]. Target 0x00488590 calls CreateDirectoryA(path, NULL) once; it does not recursively create parent directories.
//! `0x80:0x29` `Sys80_29_RemoveDirectory`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[path: Shift-JIS path]. Target 0x004885C0 calls RemoveDirectoryA directly.
//! `0x80:0x2A` `Sys80_2A_DirectoryExists`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[path: Shift-JIS path]. Target 0x004885F0 returns bit 4 of GetFileAttributesA when attributes are valid, otherwise zero.
//! `0x80:0x2B` `Sys80_2B_SplitPath`: inputs=5, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[drive_out: BP char buffer or null; directory_out: BP char buffer or null; filename_out: BP char buffer or null; extension_out: BP char buffer or null; source_path: Shift-JIS path or null]. Target 0x00488630 converts the source through MultiByteToWideChar, calls _wsplitpath, and converts requested components back to multibyte buffers. The previous ConvertDebugRecord label was incorrect.
//! `0x80:0x2C` `Sys80_2C_GetFileAttributes`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[path: Shift-JIS path]. Target 0x004886A0 forwards GetFileAttributesA unchanged.
//! `0x80:0x2D` `Sys80_2D_SetFileAttributes`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[path: Shift-JIS path; attributes: u32 Win32 attribute mask]. Target 0x004886D0 passes the path and complete attribute mask to SetFileAttributesA.
//! `0x80:0x2F` `Sys80_2F_CopyFile`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: Shift-JIS path; source: Shift-JIS path]. Target 0x00488700 clears FILE_ATTRIBUTE_READONLY on an existing destination, then calls CopyFileA(source, destination, FALSE).
//! `0x80:0x30` `Sys80_30_ReadFileBytes`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: BP byte-buffer pointer; archive_or_root: Shift-JIS string or null; file: Shift-JIS resource path]. Target 0x00488750/sub_465AB0 resolves the file against configured roots, fills the destination record/buffer and returns the loaded size.
//! `0x80:0x31` `Sys80_31_ReadFileRange`: inputs=5, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: BP byte-buffer pointer; secondary_root: Shift-JIS path or null; file: Shift-JIS resource path; offset: u32 byte offset; length: u32 byte count]. Target 0x00488790 packs offset/length for sub_465C30. Zero/zero copies the whole file; 2 denotes range overflow, 3 invalid length, 5 read/decode failure, and 6 a source larger than 64 MiB.
//! `0x80:0x32` `Sys80_32_WriteFileBytes`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[path: Shift-JIS path; source: BP byte-buffer pointer; length: u32 byte count]. Target 0x004887F0 returns whether sub_465E30 wrote exactly the requested byte count.
//! `0x80:0x33` `Sys80_33_DeleteFile`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[root: Shift-JIS path or null; file: Shift-JIS relative path]. Target 0x00488840 constructs either root\\file or primary_root+file, then calls DeleteFileA.
//! `0x80:0x34` `Sys80_34_FileExists`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[archive: Shift-JIS archive/root; file: Shift-JIS resource path]. Target 0x004888C0 pops file first and archive/root second, then calls sub_4665C0 with ECX=file and the archive/root stack argument; both values participate in loose-file and archive lookup.
//! `0x80:0x35` `Sys80_35_FileSize`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[archive: Shift-JIS archive/root; file: Shift-JIS resource path]. Target 0x00488900 pops file first and archive/root second, then calls sub_4662E0 with ECX=archive/root and file on the stack; the helper returns zero on failure.
//! `0x80:0x36` `Sys80_36_SetAdditionalResourceSearch`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[enabled: boolean i32]. Target sub_465240 stores the value in dword_506BE0; it is a mode flag, not a commit operation.
//! `0x80:0x37` `Sys80_37_PrependResourceSearchPath`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[path: Shift-JIS path]. Target allocates a path node and prepends it to the linked list rooted at dword_566630.
//! `0x80:0x38` `Sys80_38_RegisterCompositeArchive`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[name: Shift-JIS archive name; components: pointer to zero-terminated string-pointer array]. Target consumes a zero-terminated pointer array and constructs/registers a named DCArchiveComplex.
//! `0x80:0x39` `Sys80_39_SetValidatedFileRoot`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[path: Shift-JIS path]. Target accepts an existing directory and stores it with a trailing backslash in byte_518978.
//! `0x80:0x3A` `Sys80_3A_GetSpecialFolder`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: BP char buffer; mode: i32 enum 0..=5]. Target selects six Win32 system/shell folder sources, including ProgramFilesDir from the registry, and copies the resulting path.
//! `0x80:0x3B` `Sys80_3B_OpenFileDialog`: inputs=6, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[initial_directory: Shift-JIS path; description: Shift-JIS string; extension: Shift-JIS extension; destination: BP char buffer; title: Shift-JIS string; mode: i32 enum 0..=1]. Target builds one extension filter and calls GetOpenFileNameA/GetSaveFileNameA. The portable host now invokes a blocking native/scripted chooser on macOS, Windows and Linux while preserving target status codes.
//! `0x80:0x3C` `Sys80_3C_RequireResourceFile`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[file: Shift-JIS resource path; ignored_context: Shift-JIS string; message: Shift-JIS prompt text]. Target repeatedly searches configured roots and prompts Retry/Quit. The portable host performs the same loop through native macOS, Windows, or Linux message dialogs.
//! `0x80:0x3D` `Sys80_3D_GetConfiguredRoot`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: BP char buffer; kind: i32 enum 0..=1]. Target 0x00488B20/sub_4649A0 copies the primary root for kind 0, or the configured secondary root for kind 1; other values fail.
//! `0x80:0x3E` `Sys80_3E_SetPrimaryRoot`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[path: Shift-JIS path]. Target 0x00488B50 accepts only an existing directory, writes path plus a trailing backslash to the primary global root buffer and returns one.
//! `0x80:0x3F` `Sys80_3F_ConfigureRemovableArchive`: inputs=4, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[archive_name: Shift-JIS marker/archive name; subdirectory: Shift-JIS relative directory; prompt: Shift-JIS prompt text; retry: boolean i32]. Target scans removable/CD drives for the configured archive marker and stores the successful drive/subdirectory as the secondary root. The portable host scans platform mount roots and preserves the retry loop.
//! `0x80:0x40` `Sys80_40_LoadProgramModule`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[archive: Shift-JIS archive; file: Shift-JIS BP filename]. Target sub_488C00/sub_444CE0 appends decoded BP code to the current CThread and returns the previous code-used end; it does not return an object handle.
//! `0x80:0x41` `Sys80_41_FreeLastProgramModule`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[legacy_descriptor_slot: ignored ABI slot]. Target sub_444D80 removes the tail module record and rolls back CThread code-used state. The handler performs no native argument pop despite the legacy ABI descriptor count.
//! `0x80:0x44` `Sys80_44_LoadProgramThread`: inputs=5, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[archive: Shift-JIS archive; file: Shift-JIS BP filename; operand_slots: i32 count; code_bytes: i32 byte count; data_bytes: i32 byte count]. Target creates a child CThread, allocates its regions, appends the initial module and returns CThread+8.
//! `0x80:0x45` `Sys80_45_RtcNoop`: inputs=0, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[none]. The release-image selector table points at __RTC_NumErrors, but the BP ABI exposes no output and no useful engine side effect.
//! `0x80:0x46` `Sys80_46_CurrentThreadId`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[none]. Target sub_488D80 returns the current CThread field at +8.
//! `0x80:0x47` `Sys80_47_ThreadExists`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[thread_id: i32 CThread identifier]. Target recursively searches the CThread tree; identifier zero is never reported as present.
//! `0x80:0x48` `Sys80_48_EnqueueMessage`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[thread_or_program: thread/program handle; message: DWORD/BP value]. Target slot 0x00504420 calls BPThread_EnqueueDword and appends one value to CThread+0x5C/+0x60 FIFO state.
//! `0x80:0x49` `Sys80_49_DequeueMessage`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[output_ptr: BP pointer to DWORD/value]. Target slot 0x00504424 calls BPThread_DequeueDword, writes one value through output_ptr, and reports whether a value was available.
//! `0x80:0x4A` `Sys80_4A_EnqueueMessageArray`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[thread_or_program: thread/program handle; message_count: i32 count; messages_ptr: BP pointer to DWORD/value array]. Target handler appends an array by repeatedly invoking the confirmed one-value FIFO enqueue helper.
//! `0x80:0x4B` `Sys80_4B_DequeueMessageArray`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[max_count: i32 count; output_ptr: BP pointer to DWORD/value array]. Target handler performs bounded FIFO dequeue and returns the number written to output_ptr.
//! `0x80:0x4C` `Sys80_4C_InvokeThreadCallback`: inputs=4, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[thread_or_program: thread/program handle; arg1: DWORD/BP value; arg2: DWORD/BP value; arg3: DWORD/BP value]. Target BPThread_InvokeCallback reads the callback object at CThread+0x58 and invokes it with three values.
//! `0x80:0x50` `Sys80_50_SetSystemWaitState`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[value: i32 global system state]. Target 0x00489030 pops one i32 and sub_4319B0 stores it unchanged in dword_507688. The native C return value 1 is not a BP stack output.
//! `0x80:0x52` `Sys80_52_SetMainLoopWaitOverride`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[value: i32]. Target handler 0x00489050 leaves the popped i32 in EAX and sub_48D1B0 stores it in dword_503EF8; sub_48D1C0 is consumed by the executable main-loop pacing branch.
//! `0x80:0x53` `Sys80_53_ArmNextBinaryAsync`: inputs=0, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[none]. Target handler 0x00489070 stores one in dword_5668A0. Sys81:30 and Graph90:F6 consume and reset this one-shot flag when selecting DCProcReadBinary or DCProcDecodeBMV.
//! `0x80:0x54` `WaitWndMsg`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=yes, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[arg0: unrecovered BP value]. Target sub_489080 pops the message id, allocates 0x24 bytes, constructs CProcWaitWndMsg through sub_43D4D0, and registers the waiter through sub_499F40. The virtual poll consumes the matching signaled waiter and pushes lParam followed by wParam.
//! `0x80:0x58` `SetThreadTimer`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[arg0: unrecovered BP value]. Target sub_489100 pops duration and sub_445290 writes CThread+0x84 = current_tick + duration.
//! `0x80:0x59` `Sys80_59_SetAndQueryThreadTimer`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[duration_ms: i32 milliseconds]. Target 0x00489120 calls sub_4452B0 to set the CThread deadline, then sub_445260 and pushes whether the remaining time is nonzero.
//! `0x80:0x5A` `WaitTiming`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=yes, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[none]. Target sub_489160 obtains remaining time through sub_445260; only a positive value constructs CProcWaitTiming, while the Boolean result is pushed immediately on every path.
//! `0x80:0x5C` `WaitTimingOrInput`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=yes, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[duration_ms: i32 milliseconds; input_enabled: bool/i32; input_scope: i32 mask]. Target sub_4891F0 pops scope, input flag, duration and installs CProcWaitTimingEx (sub_43D2E0): deadline = engine tick + duration in the procedure (not the 0x80:0x5A thread timer); with input enabled the packed scope is registered like 0x80:0x18 and primed. Tick sub_43D430 pushes 0 on deadline, cleared dword_507688, callback code 0 or 1, and 1 on input bits & (dword_507690|0x80000181); the destructor unregisters the scope.
//! `0x80:0x5D` `Sys80_5D_SetExclusiveThread`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[enabled: bool/i32]. Target handler 0x00489290 stores either the current CThread pointer or null through sub_48D170 and mirrors whether exclusive scheduling is enabled.
//! `0x80:0x5E` `Sys80_5E_SwitchThread`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=SwitchCoroutine, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[program: program/thread handle]. Activates the target coroutine and ends the caller's current cooperative slice.
//! `0x80:0x5F` `Sys80_5F_Yield`: inputs=0, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Yield, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[none]. Target sub_4892D0 returns native interpreter status 1 without BP stack or CThread state changes. The outer interpreter ends the current cooperative pass and resumes at the next instruction.
//! `0x80:0x60` `Sys80_60_ConfigureDisplayMode`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[mode: i32 display mode 0..=7; adapter: i32 adapter 0..=1; fullscreen: bool/i32]. Target handler 0x004892E0 pops fullscreen, adapter, then mode and calls sub_461110(mode, adapter, fullscreen); adapter>=2 or mode>=8 is fatal.
//! `0x80:0x61` `Sys80_61_QueryFullscreen`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[none]. Target handler 0x00489340 pushes sub_45F640(), the current fullscreen state.
//! `0x80:0x62` `Sys80_62_ConfigureFullscreenHotkeys`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[enabled: bool/i32; descriptor_list: BP pointer to zero-terminated i32 list]. Target handler 0x00489360 passes an enable flag and zero-terminated descriptor list to sub_461740. The list may contain at most fifteen nonzero entries.
//! `0x80:0x63` `Sys80_63_SetAspectPreservingScaling`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[enabled: bool/i32]. Target handler 0x004893A0 calls sub_45E860(argument==0): zero selects stretch mode 1; nonzero selects aspect-preserving fit mode 0.
//! `0x80:0x64` `Sys80_64_SetWindowVisible`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[enabled: bool/i32]. Target handler 0x004893C0 calls sub_49A170 and then clears transient input state through sub_46DA20.
//! `0x80:0x65` `Sys80_65_MinimizeWindow`: inputs=0, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[none]. Target handler 0x004893E0 minimizes the parent window, clears transient input and sets the minimize latch.
//! `0x80:0x66` `Sys80_66_SetWindowTitle`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[text: Shift-JIS string]. Target handler 0x00489400 calls SetWindowTextA and persists the title in the engine's 256-byte title buffer on success.
//! `0x80:0x67` `Sys80_67_SetCursorIndex`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[cursor_index: i32 enum 0..=4]. Target handler 0x00489430 validates 0..=4 and stores the index used by WM_SETCURSOR.
//! `0x80:0x68` `Sys80_68_SetNativeCloseMode`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[enabled: bool/i32]. Target sub_49A0D0 stores the value and updates SC_CLOSE. Zero intercepts WM_CLOSE into an engine event; nonzero permits native close processing.
//! `0x80:0x69` `Sys80_69_RequestWindowClose`: inputs=0, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[none]. Target handler 0x004894B0 calls PostMessageA(hWndParent, WM_CLOSE, 0, 0). Portable frontends defer the request until the current scheduler pass returns, then run the same Sys80:68 close-mode gate: mode 0 queues native event `[2,0,0]` for sysmsg._bp, while nonzero allows host-window termination.
//! `0x80:0x6A` `Sys80_6A_TerminateInterpreter`: inputs=0, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=TerminateInterpreter, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[none]. Target handler returns native interpreter status 6. The outer runtime treats this as interpreter termination; it is not a resumable cooperative yield.
//! `0x80:0x6B` `Sys80_6B_SelectBootstrap`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=SwitchCoroutine, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[root_or_archive_path: Shift-JIS path; archive_namespace: Shift-JIS string]. Target handler 0x004894E0 configures the primary root/archive pair through sub_4650F0 and returns interpreter status 5 to re-enter bootstrap selection.
//! `0x80:0x6C` `Sys80_6C_SetFileDropEnabled`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[enabled: bool/i32]. Target sub_463A80 stores the flag, calls DragAcceptFiles and clears the pending dropped-file buffer.
//! `0x80:0x6D` `Sys80_6D_QueryDroppedFile`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: BP char buffer]. Target sub_463AE0 copies the pending dropped path and returns one when enabled and nonempty. Querying does not clear the native buffer.
//! `0x80:0x6E` `Sys80_6E_SetRasterWaitEnabled`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[enabled: bool/i32]. Target handler 0x00489560 stores the raw value in dword_507220, which gates the raster/vblank wait path.
//! `0x80:0x6F` `Sys80_6F_QueryDisplayAspectMismatch`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[none]. Target sub_461550 compares the desktop aspect ratio with the configured game/base aspect after scaling both by 10000.
//! `0x80:0x70` `Sys80_70_AllocateGlobalConfig`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[shift: i32 0..=12]. Target handler validates shift<=12, allocates 4096<<shift bytes, frees the previous buffer and zero-fills the replacement.
//! `0x80:0x71` `Sys80_71_ClearGlobalConfig`: inputs=0, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[none]. Target handler zeroes exactly the currently allocated global-config byte count.
//! `0x80:0x74` `Sys80_74_SetSaveDataIntegrity`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[enabled: bool/i32]. Target handler stores the raw integer in dword_506BDC. Zero alone disables save-slot encryption/checking.
//! `0x80:0x78` `Sys80_78_SaveConfigSlot`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[slot: i32; label: Shift-JIS string shorter than 40 bytes]. Target writes BGI%04d.cad as a 64-byte SYSTEMTIME/label header followed by the whole global-config buffer. Labels of 40 bytes or more are fatal.
//! `0x80:0x79` `Sys80_79_LoadConfigSlot`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[slot: i32]. Target loads and optionally decrypts the slot, applies its payload, then restores the first 1024 global-config bytes. Status: 0 success, 1 missing/empty, 2 wrong length, 3 integrity failure.
//! `0x80:0x7A` `Sys80_7A_ReadConfigSlotHeader`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: BP pointer to 64 bytes; slot: i32]. Target copies the first 64 bytes only when the file length equals 64 plus the current global-config size. Status: 0 success, 1 missing/empty, 2 partial or wrong length.
//! `0x80:0x7B` `Sys80_7B_ValidateConfigSlot`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[slot: i32]. Target reads and optionally verifies/decrypts the complete slot without applying the payload. Status codes match Sys80_79.
//! `0x80:0x80` `Sys80_80_LoadGlobalUserData`: inputs=0, outputs=3, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[none]. Target loads BGI.gdb, decodes SDC data and maps missing/decode failures to status 1/2.
//! `0x80:0x81` `Sys80_81_SaveGlobalUserData`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[none]. Target writes the BURIKO GDB 3.00 header, global data, resource names and read-flag tables to BGI.gdb.
//! `0x80:0x82` `Sys80_82_WriteGlobalDataBlock`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[offset: i32 byte offset; buffer: BP pointer; length: i32 byte count]. Target copies into the fixed 1 MiB global data region and treats zero/out-of-range transfers as fatal.
//! `0x80:0x83` `Sys80_83_ReadGlobalDataBlock`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[offset: i32 byte offset; buffer: BP pointer; length: i32 byte count]. Target copies from the fixed 1 MiB global data region and treats zero/out-of-range transfers as fatal.
//! `0x80:0x84` `Sys80_84_InternResourceName`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[name: Shift-JIS string]. Target handler 0x004899B0 calls sub_46B430, which interns the name and then returns one. The table's stable index remains internal and is not returned to BP code.
//! `0x80:0x85` `Sys80_85_ResourceNameExists`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[name: Shift-JIS string]. Target handler 0x004899E0 performs lookup only and must not insert missing names.
//! `0x80:0x88` `Sys80_88_CreateOrResizeReadFlagTable`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[name: Shift-JIS string; bit_count: i32 bit count]. Target handler 0x00489A10 calls ReadFlagTable_CreateOrResize. It is not a scenario-code preprocessing syscall.
//! `0x80:0x89` `Sys80_89_SetReadFlagBit`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[name: Shift-JIS string; bit_offset: i32 bit index; enabled: bool/i32]. Target handler 0x00489A40 changes one bit in a named compact bitset.
//! `0x80:0x8A` `Sys80_8A_SetReadFlagRange`: inputs=4, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[name: Shift-JIS string; start_bit: i32 bit index; enabled: bool/i32; bit_count: i32 bit count]. Target handler 0x00489AC0 calls ReadFlagTable_SetRange at 0x00446D40 and validates the complete range.
//! `0x80:0x8B` `Sys80_8B_QueryReadFlagBit`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[name: Shift-JIS string; output_ptr: BP pointer to i32; bit_offset: i32 bit index]. Target handler 0x00489B80 writes the queried bit through a BP pointer and returns a separate status.
//! `0x80:0x90` `Sys80_90_ResetStructuredHistory`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[capacity: i32 record count]. Frees all native 0x40-byte history nodes, clears head/tail/count and stores the new capacity.
//! `0x80:0x91` `Sys80_91_StructuredHistoryCount`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[none]. Returns the process-global bounded history count.
//! `0x80:0x94` `Sys80_94_AppendStructuredHistoryFields`: inputs=13, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[value0: i32; value1: i32; value2: i32; value3: i32; value4: i32; value5: i32; value6: i32; value7: i32; value8: i32; short_text1: Shift-JIS string; short_text2: Shift-JIS string; short_text3: Shift-JIS string; text: Shift-JIS string]. Allocates a native history node, validates 31/255-byte string limits, appends at the tail and evicts the oldest record at capacity.
//! `0x80:0x95` `Sys80_95_ReadStructuredHistory`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[output_ptr: BP pointer to record; newest_index: u32 index]. Index zero selects the newest record; writes the target record layout without the extended field.
//! `0x80:0x96` `Sys80_96_AppendStructuredHistoryRecord`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[record_ptr: BP pointer to record]. Imports the target scalar/string record layout, including the optional extended text at byte 512.
//! `0x80:0x97` `Sys80_97_ReadStructuredHistoryExtended`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[output_ptr: BP pointer to record; newest_index: u32 index]. Same newest-first lookup as 0x95 and additionally copies the optional extended text.
//! `0x80:0x98` `Sys80_98_IndexedRecordOpen`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[handle_output: BP pointer to i32; capacity: u32 record count; record_size: u32 byte count]. Creates a capacity-bounded fixed-record table and writes a monotonically allocated integer identifier.
//! `0x80:0x99` `Sys80_99_IndexedRecordClose`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[handle: i32 table identifier]. Closes an indexed-record table; missing identifiers return one.
//! `0x80:0x9A` `Sys80_9A_IndexedRecordCount`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[output_ptr: BP pointer to i32; handle: i32 table identifier]. Writes the current record count through the output pointer.
//! `0x80:0x9C` `Sys80_9C_IndexedRecordPush`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[handle: i32 table identifier; source: BP pointer]. Copies one fixed-size record to the front and truncates records beyond capacity.
//! `0x80:0x9D` `Sys80_9D_IndexedRecordLoad`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[output_ptr: BP pointer; handle: i32 table identifier; index: u32 newest-first index]. Loads one newest-first record; missing table is one and invalid index is two.
//! `0x80:0x9E` `Sys80_9E_IndexedRecordRemove`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[handle: i32 table identifier; start: u32 newest-first index; count: u32 record count]. Removes up to count records starting at a newest-first index.
//! `0x80:0xA0` `Sys80_A0_PollQueuedEvent`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[output_ptr: BP pointer to three i32 values]. Pops the oldest process-global three-DWORD event into caller memory.
//! `0x80:0xA1` `Sys80_A1_PostQueuedEvent`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[event_code: i32; parameter: i32]. Queues [0,event_code,parameter] in the target critical-section protected FIFO.
//! `0x80:0xA8` `Sys80_A8_SetRegisteredObjectState`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[object_id: i32 registry identifier; state: i32]. Looks up a DCIndProc registry entry and writes its state field at native offset +0x10.
//! `0x80:0xA9` `Sys80_A9_GetRegisteredObjectState`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[object_id: i32 registry identifier; output_ptr: BP pointer to i32]. Looks up a registered object and writes its current state through the output pointer.
//! `0x80:0xAC` `Sys80_AC_QueueRegisteredObjectMessage`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[object_id: i32 registry identifier; count: i32 DWORD count 1..=256; descriptor: BP pointer to DWORD array]. Returns zero only when registry lookup fails. For an existing object, a 1..=256 DWORD descriptor is queued; an invalid count queues nothing but still returns one, matching sub_48A250.
//! `0x80:0xAF` `Sys80_AF_SetSystemModeFlag`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[mode: i32 0..=1]. Accepts only zero or one and stores the process-global mode queried by the System81 extension.
//! `0x80:0xB0` `Sys80_B0_CreateExclusionSection`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[name: Shift-JIS string; capacity: i32]. Creates a named capacity-limited CExclusion section; duplicate names return zero.
//! `0x80:0xB1` `Sys80_B1_DeleteExclusionSection`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[name: Shift-JIS string]. Returns 0x80000001 when missing and 0x80000002 while holders or waiters remain.
//! `0x80:0xB4` `Sys80_B4_WaitExclusionSection`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=yes, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[name: Shift-JIS string; priority: u32]. Installs CProcExclusion, queues the current thread by descending priority and resumes only when it is queue head and capacity is available.
//! `0x80:0xB5` `Sys80_B5_LeaveExclusionSection`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[name: Shift-JIS string]. Releases one holder entry for the current thread; missing/not-owner map to 0x80000001/0x80000003.
//! `0x80:0xB6` `Sys80_B6_QueryExclusionSection`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[name: Shift-JIS string; priority: u32]. Returns zero when capacity covers current holders plus all queued priorities greater than or equal to the request, otherwise 0x80000004.
//! `0x80:0xC0` `Sys80_C0_EncodeData`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=yes, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: BP pointer; source: BP pointer; length: u32 bytes]. Target handler constructs CProcEncodeData from destination, source, and length; completion publishes the encoded length.
//! `0x80:0xC1` `Sys80_C1_DecodeSdcBuffer`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: BP pointer; source: BP pointer]. Exact 0x0048A4D0 saves the first native pop in ESI and passes it in EAX as the SDC source to sub_4938F0; the second pop is its destination argument.
//! `0x80:0xC4` `Sys80_C4_EncodeStructArray`: inputs=4, outputs=0, procedure=yes, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: BP pointer; source: BP pointer; record_size: u32 bytes; record_count: u32]. Target handler constructs CProcEncodeStruct, applying DCFS record transform and SDC compression asynchronously.
//! `0x80:0xC5` `Sys80_C5_DecodeStructArray`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: BP pointer; source: BP pointer]. Target handler synchronously performs SDC decompression followed by DCFS reconstruction and returns the record count.
//! `0x80:0xCF` `Sys80_CF_DecodeData`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=yes, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: BP pointer; source: BP pointer; requested_length: u32 bytes]. Target constructs DCProcDecodeData. SDC streams are exact; the non-SDC target decoder remains represented by a bounded raw-copy compatibility path.
//! `0x80:0xD0` `Sys80_D0_RecordTableOpen`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[handle_out: BP pointer to i32; record_size: i32 bytes]. Target allocates an integer-handle keyed table whose entries are separately allocated record nodes; there is no fixed table capacity. Record sizes <=1 return 0x80000001.
//! `0x80:0xD1` `Sys80_D1_RecordTableClose`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[handle: integer handle]. Target removes the integer-handle table; a missing table returns 0x80000002.
//! `0x80:0xD2` `Sys80_D2_RecordTableInsert`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[handle: integer handle; key: Shift-JIS string; source: BP pointer]. Target inserts a separately allocated fixed-size record node or replaces the existing node selected by string key.
//! `0x80:0xD3` `Sys80_D3_RecordTableRemove`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[handle: integer handle; key: Shift-JIS string]. Target distinguishes missing table from missing key.
//! `0x80:0xD4` `Sys80_D4_RecordTableFetch`: inputs=4, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: BP pointer; handle: integer handle; key: nullable Shift-JIS pointer; index: i32]. Target fetches by key or linked-list insertion-order index and copies the fixed-size record.
//! `0x80:0xD8` `Sys80_D8_ClearStringNamespaces`: inputs=0, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[none]. Target clears all string namespaces except protected table id 0x80000000.
//! `0x80:0xD9` `Sys80_D9_StringNamespaceCount`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[table_id: i32]. Target returns the number of interned strings in one namespace.
//! `0x80:0xDA` `Sys80_DA_ReplaceStringNamespace`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[table_id: i32; count: i32; source: BP pointer]. Target replaces a namespace from a packed string sequence or removes it when count is zero.
//! `0x80:0xDB` `Sys80_DB_SerializeStringNamespace`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: nullable BP pointer; table_id: i32]. Target serializes one namespace including each NUL terminator.
//! `0x80:0xDC` `Sys80_DC_InternStringNamespace`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[table_id: i32; value: Shift-JIS string]. Target interns/appends a string in one namespace with no graph-resource side effect.
//! `0x80:0xDD` `Sys80_DD_CopyIndexedNamespaceEntry`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: BP pointer to byte buffer; table_id: i32 namespace identifier; index: i32 record index]. Target handler 0x0048A900 passes destination/table/index to sub_495850. The helper locates the 12-byte metadata slot, then copies the entry payload pointer by its stored byte length; sub_495550 constructs those payloads as Shift-JIS strings including the terminating NUL. Missing table/index map to 0x80000001/0x80000002.
//! `0x80:0xDE` `Sys80_DE_StringNamespaceEntryLength`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[length_out: BP pointer to i32; table_id: i32; index: i32]. Target reports the encoded byte length of one namespace entry without copying it.
//! `0x80:0xE0` `Sys80_E0_LaunchProcessWait`: inputs=4, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[working_directory: Shift-JIS string; command_line: Shift-JIS string; error_message: Shift-JIS string; restore_parent: bool/i32]. Target launches a process, waits for it, and optionally restores the parent window.
//! `0x80:0xE1` `Sys80_E1_RestartWithCommand`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=TerminateInterpreter, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[working_directory: nullable Shift-JIS pointer; command_line: non-null Shift-JIS pointer; error_message: nullable Shift-JIS pointer]. Target accepts nullable working/error pointers, requires a non-null command pointer, stores restart fields, destroys the main window, returns native control status 6, and launches after WinMain cleanup.
//! `0x80:0xE2` `Sys80_E2_LaunchProcessWaitUninstaller`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[working_directory: Shift-JIS string; command_line: Shift-JIS string; error_message: Shift-JIS string]. Target launches and waits, then additionally waits for the named uninstaller synchronization object.
//! `0x80:0xE3` `Sys80_E3_ShellOpen`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[target: Shift-JIS string]. Target invokes ShellExecute with the open verb.
//! `0x80:0xE8` `Sys80_E8_WriteGameId`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: BP pointer]. Target writes the literal Tayutama2TV string.
//! `0x80:0xE9` `Sys80_E9_HashFile`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[hash_out: BP pointer to 8 bytes; path: Shift-JIS string]. Target hashes bytes with h=byte+233*h and four rolling tail accumulators.
//! `0x80:0xEA` `Sys80_EA_SetUninstallerProduct`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[product: Shift-JIS string]. Target formats and stores the mutex name `Uninstaller for <product> is executing.` used by the uninstaller wait loop.
//! `0x80:0xF0` `Sys80_F0_ShowInputDialog`: inputs=8, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[initial_text: Shift-JIS string; output_value1: BP pointer to i32; output_value2: BP pointer to i32; output_text: BP character buffer; option_value1: i32; option_value2: i32; mode: i32; caption: Shift-JIS string]. Target sub_471FB0 edits one Shift-JIS buffer plus two DWORD options. VM mediation now preserves all three output writes while the host supplies a cross-platform modal editor.
//! `0x80:0xF1` `Sys80_F1_ShowInstallerDialog`: inputs=6, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[text1: Shift-JIS string; text2: nullable Shift-JIS string; text3: Shift-JIS string; text4: Shift-JIS string; mode1: i32; mode2: i32]. Target sub_472050 opens one of two installer dialog resources using four text fields and two mode globals. Portable hosts expose the same modal success/cancel boundary.
//! `0x80:0xF2` `Sys80_F2_RunInstallerWorkflow`: inputs=14, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[root: Shift-JIS installation path; optional_directories: nullable zero-terminated string-pointer list; required_directories: zero-terminated string-pointer list; file_count: i32; metadata: Shift-JIS string/pointer; source_files: pointer to file_count Shift-JIS pointers; destination_files: pointer to file_count Shift-JIS pointers; flags: i32; format_string: Shift-JIS string; vendor: Shift-JIS string; product: Shift-JIS string; uninstall_source: nullable Shift-JIS string; prompt: Shift-JIS string; mode: i32]. Target sub_472150 creates the installation tree, copies parallel file lists, writes uninst.lst and InstalledFolder metadata. The portable host performs those operations without Win32-only dialog/resource internals.
//! `0x80:0xF3` `Sys80_F3_RunShortcutInstallerWorkflow`: inputs=8, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[target_root: Shift-JIS path; primary_target: Shift-JIS relative path; primary_shortcut_name: Shift-JIS string; secondary_target: Shift-JIS relative path; secondary_shortcut_name: Shift-JIS string; program_group: Shift-JIS string; create_program_group: bool/i32; create_desktop: bool/i32]. Target sub_471530 creates the primary desktop shortcut and up to two program-menu shortcuts from one target root and two relative targets. Portable hosts preserve the same branching and file destinations.
//! `0x80:0xF4` `Sys80_F4_RemoveUninstallListedFiles`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[root: Shift-JIS path; exclusions: pointer to NUL-terminated string-pointer array]. Target reads raw LF-separated Shift-JIS entries from root\\uninst.lst and deletes each except leading-@ directives, exact `uninst.lst`, and byte-exact exclusions.
//! `0x80:0xF5` `Sys80_F5_AppendUninstallListEntries`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[root: Shift-JIS path; entries: pointer to NUL-terminated string-pointer array]. Target requires root\\uninst.lst to exist, appends entries absent by C-string substring search, and rewrites the terminal NUL.
//! `0x80:0xF6` `Sys80_F6_RemoveInstallerShortcuts`: inputs=4, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[file_name: Shift-JIS string; secondary_file: Shift-JIS string; program_group: Shift-JIS string; remove_group: bool/i32]. Target removes desktop/program-menu shortcuts and optionally the group.
//! `0x80:0xF7` `Sys80_F7_CreateShortcut`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[program_group: nullable Shift-JIS string; shortcut_name: Shift-JIS string; target: Shift-JIS string]. Target passes ECX=0 to sub_4713F0: null group writes the desktop, non-null group writes CSIDL_PROGRAMS\\group. Hosts create .lnk on Windows and executable desktop-compatible launchers elsewhere.
//! `0x80:0xF8` `Sys80_F8_ReadInstalledFolder`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[output: BP character buffer; vendor: Shift-JIS string; product: Shift-JIS string]. Target reads HKLM Software\\vendor\\product InstalledFolder. Windows reads the native registry and all hosts fall back to the persistent platform store.
//! `0x80:0xF9` `Sys80_F9_DeleteInstalledRegistryKey`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[vendor: Shift-JIS string; product: Shift-JIS string]. Target deletes HKLM Software\\vendor\\product.
//! `0x80:0xFA` `Sys80_FA_ReadWindowsPathFile`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[output: BP character buffer; file_name: Shift-JIS string]. Target reads WindowsDir\\file and accepts only NUL-terminated content ending in a backslash before the terminator.
//! `0x80:0xFB` `Sys80_FB_WriteWindowsDirectory`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[output: BP character buffer]. Target calls sub_467570 with selector zero and writes the resulting directory. The VM writes the host special-folder result through the exact BP pointer contract.
//! `0x80:0xFC` `Sys80_FC_RegisterFileAssociation`: inputs=5, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[extension: Shift-JIS string; class_name: Shift-JIS string; description: Shift-JIS string; icon: Shift-JIS string; open_command: Shift-JIS string]. Target writes the extension/class/description/icon/open-command hierarchy under HKCR. Windows writes HKCU\\Software\\Classes; all hosts persist the equivalent association in the platform store.
//! `0x80:0xFD` `Sys80_FD_QueryLauncherMode`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[none]. Target returns the launcher-mode global established by startup. The portable runtime returns the configured launcher mode through SysApi instead of forcing a constant fallback.
//! `0x80:0xFE` `Sys80_FE_InstallerFeatureAvailable`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[none]. Target handler pushes constant 1.
//!
//! ## System extended group 0x81
//!
//! `0x81:0x04` `Sys81_04_SetClockJumpThreshold`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[threshold_ms: i32 milliseconds]. Target sub_498820 validates 50..60000 and stores the engine-clock discontinuity threshold.
//! `0x81:0x07` `Sys81_07_CopyCoordinateSlot`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[index: i32; destination: pointer to two i32]. Target sub_48E590 copies one of five two-DWORD coordinate transform slots.
//! `0x81:0x08` `Sys81_08_GetUserName`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: Shift-JIS buffer]. Target calls GetUserNameA with a 257-byte capacity.
//! `0x81:0x09` `Sys81_09_GetComputerName`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: Shift-JIS buffer]. Target calls GetComputerNameA with a 16-byte capacity.
//! `0x81:0x0A` `Sys81_0A_GetCpuBrand`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: Shift-JIS buffer]. Target sub_46F720 gates extended CPUID leaves 0x80000002..4 and normalizes whitespace.
//! `0x81:0x0B` `Sys81_0B_GetCpuDisplayInfo`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[reserved: pointer; signature: pointer to four i32; text: Shift-JIS buffer]. Target sub_45E490 normalizes CPU text and copies four cached 16-bit signature fields as DWORDs.
//! `0x81:0x0C` `Sys81_0C_GetOsVersion`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[service_pack: Shift-JIS buffer; version: pointer to four u32]. Target copies cached GetVersionExA data.
//! `0x81:0x0D` `Sys81_0D_GetPhysicalMemoryMb`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[available_mb: pointer to u32; total_mb: pointer to u32]. Target calls GlobalMemoryStatusEx and shifts both physical-memory values right by 20.
//! `0x81:0x0E` `Sys81_0E_GetAdjustedDesktopDimensions`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: pointer to two u32]. Target sub_45E580 applies the wide/tall desktop halving rules.
//! `0x81:0x0F` `Sys81_0F_IsMainWindowMinimized`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[none]. Target directly returns IsIconic(hWndParent).
//! `0x81:0x10` `Sys81_10_SwapInputBinding`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[replacement: i32; index: i32]. Target sub_46DA40 returns the old dword_518CAC[6*index] then stores the replacement.
//! `0x81:0x11` `Sys81_11_CopyKeyboardState`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: pointer to 256 bytes]. Target directly calls GetKeyboardState.
//! `0x81:0x14` `Sys81_14_SetKeyboardPollingOverride`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[enabled: i32]. Target sub_46D540 controls the raw keyboard polling override consumed by sub_46D560.
//! `0x81:0x16` `Sys81_16_ConfigurePointerHistory`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[distance: i32; capacity: i32]. Target clears the linked history and accepts capacities up to 512.
//! `0x81:0x17` `Sys81_17_CopyPointerHistory`: inputs=4, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[count: i32; start: i32; distances: pointer to i32 array; points: pointer to x/y pairs]. Target traverses the pointer-history linked list newest-first.
//! `0x81:0x18` `Sys81_18_RegisterTouchInput`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[enabled: i32]. Target calls RegisterTouchWindow or UnregisterTouchWindow for hWndParent.
//! `0x81:0x19` `Sys81_19_CopyTouchRecords`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: pointer to six-DWORD records]. Target copies each touch record as six DWORDs.
//! `0x81:0x1B` `Sys81_1B_SetControllerWakeEntry`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[value: i32; index: i32]. Target sub_460E40 writes one of 36 controller wake values.
//! `0x81:0x1D` `Sys81_1D_QueryControllerState`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: pointer to six i32; device: pointer/nullable device selector]. Target sub_460E60 aggregates DirectInput device state and clamps three axes to -1024..1024.
//! `0x81:0x1E` `Sys81_1E_InjectMouseClick`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[button_code: i32]. Target posts the matching synthetic mouse down/up messages.
//! `0x81:0x1F` `Sys81_1F_SetMessageAuxiliaryInputMask`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[mask: i32 bit mask]. Target handler 0x0048B7D0 calls sub_4319F0 and writes dword_507690. CProcDspMsg::Tick ORs this mask with 0x80000181 before filtering current input bits.
//! `0x81:0x28` `Sys81_28_OpenResourceStream`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[mode: i32; path: Shift-JIS path; handle_out: pointer to u32]. Target sub_4011B0 returns 1 invalid mode, 2 duplicate path, 3 open failure, or 0.
//! `0x81:0x29` `Sys81_29_QueueResourceClose`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[handle: integer stream handle; status_out: pointer to i32]. Target queues a close operation; missing handles map to status 4.
//! `0x81:0x2A` `Sys81_2A_QueueResourceRead`: inputs=4, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[length: i32 bytes; destination: byte buffer; handle: integer stream handle; status_out: pointer to i32]. Target sub_4014A0 queues a read request on the stream worker list.
//! `0x81:0x2B` `Sys81_2B_QueueResourceSeek`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[offset: i32; handle: integer stream handle; status_out: pointer to i32]. Target sub_4014C0 queues a no-buffer stream operation at the supplied offset.
//! `0x81:0x2C` `Sys81_2C_GetFileTimes`: inputs=4, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[path: Shift-JIS path; write_time: SYSTEMTIME pointer; access_time: SYSTEMTIME pointer; creation_time: SYSTEMTIME pointer]. Target opens the file abstraction, queries three FILETIMEs and converts each to SYSTEMTIME.
//! `0x81:0x2D` `Sys81_2D_SetFileTimes`: inputs=4, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[write_time: SYSTEMTIME pointer; access_time: SYSTEMTIME pointer; creation_time: SYSTEMTIME pointer; path: Shift-JIS path]. Target converts three SYSTEMTIMEs to FILETIME and applies them to the opened file.
//! `0x81:0x2F` `Sys81_2F_TestPathWritable`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[directory: Shift-JIS path]. Target creates, reopens and deletes a temporary file in the directory.
//! `0x81:0x30` `Sys81_30_ReadResourceBinary`: inputs=5, outputs=0, procedure=yes, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: byte buffer; archive: Shift-JIS archive/root; file: Shift-JIS file name; offset: i32 bytes; length: i32 bytes]. Target pop order is length, offset, file, archive/root, destination; an empty file name selects the archive's first entry. Named archive reads return success with the actual byte count even when it is smaller than the caller's capacity, while loose-file short reads return status 3. The one-shot async flag chooses synchronous sub_467F50 or DCProcReadBinary.
//! `0x81:0x31` `Sys81_31_InternetRead`: inputs=4, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[length: i32 bytes; offset: i32 bytes; url: Shift-JIS URL; destination: buffer/size pointer]. Target WinINet helper distinguishes initialization, open, read and short-read failures.
//! `0x81:0x32` `Sys81_32_DirectFileRead`: inputs=4, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[bytes_read: pointer to u32; path: Shift-JIS path; destination: byte buffer; length: i32 bytes]. Target uses unbuffered/direct file I/O and validates a drive-letter path.
//! `0x81:0x35` `Sys81_35_ResourceSize`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[context: pointer/reserved; path: Shift-JIS path]. Target sub_468310 returns the resource size.
//! `0x81:0x36` `Sys81_36_EnumerateDriveTypes`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: pointer to 26 i32]. Target maps GetDriveTypeA to BGI codes: fixed 1, removable 2, network 3, CD-ROM 4, RAM disk 5.
//! `0x81:0x37` `Sys81_37_GetDiskFreeMb`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[path: Shift-JIS path; destination: pointer to u32]. Target queries free bytes and shifts right by 20.
//! `0x81:0x38` `Sys81_38_ShowResourceFileDialog`: inputs=7, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[mode: i32; title: Shift-JIS text; default_name: Shift-JIS text; extension_table: pointer to DWORD string pointers; label_table: pointer to DWORD string pointers; filter_count: i32; destination: Shift-JIS buffer]. Target builds parallel filter-label and extension arrays then calls the Win32 dialog helper.
//! `0x81:0x39` `Sys81_39_EnumerateResources`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: packed NUL strings; required_bytes: pointer to u32; pattern: Shift-JIS pattern]. Target sub_467A60 enumerates matching archive/resource names into packed NUL strings.
//! `0x81:0x3A` `Sys81_3A_BrowseFolder`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[root: i32/LPARAM; title: Shift-JIS text; destination: Shift-JIS buffer]. Target opens SHBrowseForFolder and converts the selected PIDL to a path.
//! `0x81:0x3B` `Sys81_3B_ShowResourceList`: inputs=4, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[reserved: pointer; title: Shift-JIS text; pattern: Shift-JIS pattern; context: pointer]. Target enumerates resources, joins names with newlines and opens a modal list.
//! `0x81:0x3C` `Sys81_3C_ResourceExists`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[path: Shift-JIS path]. Target sub_4685D0 tests the resource abstraction rather than only the host filesystem.
//! `0x81:0x3D` `Sys81_3D_GetVolumeLabel`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[path: Shift-JIS drive/path; destination: Shift-JIS buffer]. Target sub_468670 calls GetVolumeInformationA.
//! `0x81:0x3E` `Sys81_3E_QueryDevicePowerState`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[path: Shift-JIS device/file path; destination: pointer to BOOL]. Target returns whether the query mechanism opened/succeeded and writes the device power state.
//! `0x81:0x44` `Sys81_44_CreateChildThread`: inputs=4, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[data_size: i32; code_size: i32; operand_slots: i32; entry_index: i32]. Target constructs DCTChildThread, validates sizes/index and returns CThread+8.
//! `0x81:0x60` `Sys81_60_ConfigureScreenMode`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[second: i32; first: i32; index: i32]. Target sub_461040 validates slot and nonzero dimensions.
//! `0x81:0x61` `Sys81_61_QueryEffectiveDisplayMode`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[none]. Target returns the configured mode, but mode 2 falls back to zero when adjusted desktop dimensions are too small.
//! `0x81:0x62` `Sys81_62_SetMonitorAdapterMode`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[mode: i32]. Target sub_45E830 stores the monitor/adapter selection mode.
//! `0x81:0x63` `Sys81_63_SetConfigInputMode`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[mode: i32]. Target sub_45E860 stores the display/input configuration mode.
//! `0x81:0x64` `Sys81_64_ConfigureLogicalScreenSize`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[height: i32; width: i32]. Target sub_45E770 updates logical dimensions and triggers render reconfiguration.
//! `0x81:0x65` `Sys81_65_SetWindowPositionOverride`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[value: i32]. Target value is consumed by WM_WINDOWPOSCHANGING position override logic.
//! `0x81:0x68` `Sys81_68_SwapPauseOnDeactivate`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[enabled: i32]. Target sub_498800 swaps dword_566A4C and returns the old value.
//! `0x81:0x69` `Sys81_69_SetPrintScreenHotkeyCapture`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[enabled: i32]. Target registers/unregisters sixteen PrintScreen hotkeys for modifiers 0..15.
//! `0x81:0x6A` `Sys81_6A_SetErrorCaptureMode`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[mode: i32]. Target sub_464440 selects whether engine error text is captured.
//! `0x81:0x6B` `Sys81_6B_CopyCapturedError`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: Shift-JIS buffer/nullable]. Target sub_464480 copies dword_566004 when non-null and returns strlen+1.
//! `0x81:0x6D` `Sys81_6D_QueryPixelShaderVersion`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[none]. Target sub_460590 reads the D3DCAPS9 field at offset 0xCC.
//! `0x81:0x6E` `Sys81_6E_UncaughtExceptionActive`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[none]. Target directly returns the Microsoft CRT __uncaught_exception result.
//! `0x81:0x6F` `Sys81_6F_SetBicubicShader`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[mode: i32]. Target sub_460550 manages the D3DX bicubic scaler shader.
//! `0x81:0xB0` `Sys81_B0_WideStringDistance`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[left: UTF-16 NUL string; right: UTF-16 NUL string]. Target sub_495C50 computes len(left)+len(right)-LCS(left,right).
//! `0x81:0xB7` `Sys81_B7_ShiftJisToUtf16`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[source: Shift-JIS NUL string; destination: UTF-16 buffer/nullable]. Target converts single-byte and Shift-JIS double-byte code units without a Windows normalization pass.
//! `0x81:0xD0` `Sys81_D0_BlobTableOpen`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[capacity: i32; handle_out: pointer to u32]. Target creates a growable array of {pointer,size} blob slots.
//! `0x81:0xD1` `Sys81_D1_BlobTableClose`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[handle: integer table handle]. Target removes the matching table node and frees all blobs.
//! `0x81:0xD2` `Sys81_D2_BlobTableStore`: inputs=5, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[handle: integer table handle; source: byte buffer; size: i32 bytes; requested_index: i32; index_out: pointer/nullable]. Target stores into a requested slot or the first free slot; allocation failure maps to 0x80000003.
//! `0x81:0xD3` `Sys81_D3_BlobTableRemove`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[index: i32; handle: integer table handle]. Target clears and frees one occupied slot; invalid slot maps to 0x80000004.
//! `0x81:0xD4` `Sys81_D4_BlobTableFetch`: inputs=4, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[index: i32; handle: integer table handle; size_out: pointer to u32; destination: byte buffer/nullable]. Target copies one slot and reports 0x80000004 when absent.
//! `0x81:0xD5` `Sys81_D5_BlobTableEnumerate`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[handle: integer table handle; count_out: pointer to u32; pairs_out: pointer to index/size pairs]. Target emits index/size pairs for occupied slots.
//! `0x81:0xE0` `Sys81_E0_LaunchProcessWait`: inputs=7, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[flags: i32; error_message: Shift-JIS text; show_window: i32; working_directory: Shift-JIS path; executable: Shift-JIS file; arguments: Shift-JIS command line; exit_code_out: pointer to u32/nullable]. Target sub_4724B0 launches, waits while pumping BGI messages, and optionally reads exit code.
//! `0x81:0xE9` `Sys81_E9_UpdateRollingHash`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[length: i32 bytes; source: byte buffer; state: pointer to 8 bytes]. Target sub_401900 updates a 233-multiplier DWORD plus four byte accumulators.
//! `0x81:0xEA` `Sys81_EA_Md5`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[length: i32 bytes; source: byte buffer; destination: pointer to 16 bytes]. Target sub_4A1440 pads with the MD5 constants/rounds and writes four digest DWORDs.
//! `0x81:0xEC` `Sys81_EC_CreateNamedMutex`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[name: Shift-JIS mutex name]. Target rejects pre-existing mutex names and returns a monotonic BGI handle.
//! `0x81:0xED` `Sys81_ED_ReleaseNamedMutex`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[handle: integer mutex handle]. Target releases/closes the native mutex and removes its BGI record.
//! `0x81:0xF2` `Sys81_F2_RunInstallationProcedure`: inputs=13, outputs=0, procedure=yes, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[root: Shift-JIS installation path; optional_directories: nullable zero-terminated string-pointer list; required_directories: zero-terminated string-pointer list; file_count: i32; descriptor_values: pointer to file_count DWORDs; source_files: pointer to file_count Shift-JIS pointers; destination_files: pointer to file_count Shift-JIS pointers; mode: i32; text1: Shift-JIS string; text2: Shift-JIS string; text3: Shift-JIS string; text4: Shift-JIS string; text5: Shift-JIS string]. Target sub_48C650 converts two zero-terminated directory lists, one DWORD descriptor array and two parallel file-name arrays, then constructs DCProcInstallation. Status zero installs the procedure; 0x80000000..2 map to immediate 1..3. The portable host performs the same file/directory setup synchronously and releases the VM through a target-shaped DCProcInstallation boundary.
//! `0x81:0xF7` `Sys81_F7_CreateSpecialFolderShortcut`: inputs=4, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[program_group: nullable Shift-JIS string; shortcut_name: Shift-JIS string; target: Shift-JIS string; special_folder_mode: i32]. Wrapper 0x0048C8D0 forwards a special-folder selector in ECX plus optional group, shortcut name, and target to sub_4713F0; the portable host creates a native or desktop-compatible shortcut in the selected folder.
//!
//! ## Graph group 0x90
//!
//! `0x90:0x00` `Graph90_00_RequestRedraw`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[full_redraw: boolean]. Target helpers sub_461D70/sub_461D80 coalesce pending redraw requests and preserve the stronger full-redraw request.
//! `0x90:0x01` `Graph90_01_SetSchedulerGate`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[gate: i32]. Target stores the supplied graph scheduler gate without converting it to an unrelated rendering property.
//! `0x90:0x02` `Graph90_02_SetFrameRate`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[frames_per_second: i32 1..=1000]. Target validates 1..=1000, derives the millisecond interval, and resets its next frame deadline.
//! `0x90:0x03` `Graph90_03_InitializeBitmapMemoryManager`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[byte_limit: i32 0..=0x20000000]. Target validates the byte limit and initializes/resets the native bitmap memory manager. Portable runtime enforces the limit but does not reproduce the allocator layout.
//! `0x90:0x04` `Graph90_04_CreateWorkBitmap`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[bitmap: bitmap handle <0x4000]. Target allocates a work bitmap using current display dimensions and native format.
//! `0x90:0x05` `Graph90_05_CreatePrioritizedWorkBitmap`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[bitmap: bitmap handle <0x4000; priority: u16 render priority]. Target creates a work bitmap and registers its 16-bit render priority.
//! `0x90:0x06` `Graph90_06_SetCenter`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[x: i32 coordinate; y: i32 coordinate]. Target sub_461E30/sub_442E70 stores an optional graph centre. The manager default is (-1,-1); sub_442E90 only accepts coordinates inside the current display, and normal Sprite projection sub_429AF0 uses a valid centre instead of display_width/2,display_height/2 when CDspObj+0x100 is enabled.
//! `0x90:0x07` `Graph90_07_SetDefaultProcedureDuration`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[duration: i32 time value]. Target stores the default duration used by later graph control procedures.
//! `0x90:0x08` `Graph90_08_SetDisplayEnabled`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[enabled: i32 gate]. Target stores the enable gate and invalidates/rechecks the display chain.
//! `0x90:0x09` `Graph90_09_SetDefaultPriority`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[priority: u16 render priority]. Target validates and stores the default graph priority.
//! `0x90:0x0A` `Graph90_0A_SetObjectUpdateRedrawPolicy`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[enabled: boolean; full_redraw: boolean]. Target writes two globals controlling redraw requests after display-object update completion; it is not a global coordinate offset.
//! `0x90:0x0B` `Graph90_0B_SetCurrentBitmap`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[bitmap: bitmap handle]. Target writes the supplied bitmap handle to the bitmap manager current slot; it is not the current display object.
//! `0x90:0x0C` `Graph90_0C_SetDisplayOptions`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[setting: i32; mode: i32 <=256]. Target stores two display settings and invalidates sixteen display-object records.
//! `0x90:0x0D` `Graph90_0D_SetRasterFormatMode`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[mode: i32 0..=3]. Target derives layouts (2,1,2), (4,2,4), (6,3,8), or (8,4,16) and rebuilds registered fonts.
//! `0x90:0x0E` `Graph90_0E_RegisterFont`: inputs=5, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[font_name_id: string/name id; height: i32 4..=200; weight_percent: i32 25..=200; italic: boolean; font_id: i32 >=2]. Target deduplicates by face/height/weight/italic and updates the registered font id.
//! `0x90:0x0F` `Graph90_0F_SetBitmapUnblendColor`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[rgb: packed RGB color]. Target stores the packed RGB color used by bitmap alpha-unblend paths.
//! `0x90:0x10` `Graph90_10_LoadBitmap`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=yes, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[bitmap: bitmap handle; archive: Shift-JIS archive name; resource: Shift-JIS resource name]. Target uses a synchronous cache hit path or installs CProcLoadBitmap and returns native scheduler status 2. CBG loading preserves the native image-header format selected by `sub_401C10`: 8bpp->3, 16bpp->0, 24bpp is rewritten by `sub_469EE0` to 32bpp/subtype 7 then normalized by `sub_407DA0` to format 1, while 32bpp subtype 4/5/7 selects 4/5/7 (7 normalizes to 1) and other 32bpp subtypes select format 2. Cached/preloaded pixels retain this native format when later bound to a bitmap handle.
//! `0x90:0x11` `Graph90_11_CreateBitmap`: inputs=4, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[bitmap: bitmap handle; width: i32 pixels; height: i32 pixels; format: native bitmap format]. Target creates a bitmap with explicit dimensions and format.
//! `0x90:0x12` `Graph90_12_ReleaseBitmap`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[bitmap: bitmap handle]. Target releases one bitmap registry slot and pushes success.
//! `0x90:0x13` `Graph90_13_FillBitmap`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[bitmap: bitmap handle; color: packed color]. Target clears/fills the selected bitmap with the supplied packed color.
//! `0x90:0x14` `Graph90_14_CreateBitmapFromPixels`: inputs=5, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[bitmap: bitmap handle; width: i32 pixels; height: i32 pixels; format: native bitmap format; pixels: BP pointer]. Target creates a bitmap from caller memory. The VM bridge preserves BP memory ownership and byte count.
//! `0x90:0x15` `Graph90_15_CopyBitmapPixels`: inputs=4, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: BP pointer; written: BP i32 pointer; capacity: i32 bytes; bitmap: bitmap handle]. Target copies bitmap bytes to caller memory subject to capacity and writes the copied count.
//! `0x90:0x16` `Graph90_16_QueryBitmapInfo`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[info: BP pointer to 6 DWORD record; bitmap: bitmap handle]. sub_479C00/sub_407F20 write [pixels, row_stride, width, height, format, bytes_per_pixel], then the public wrapper clears pixels at +0. The portable registry reproduces ordinary bitmap records; external-DIB orientation remapping remains partial.
//! `0x90:0x17` `Graph90_17_ValidateBitmapFormat`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[bitmap: bitmap handle; expected_format: native bitmap format]. Target returns 0 for compatible, 1 for missing, and 2 for incompatible, with its format-2 to format-1 conversion allowance.
//! `0x90:0x18` `Graph90_18_BlitBitmap`: inputs=6, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[arg0: i32 / bitmap operand; arg1: i32 / bitmap operand; arg2: i32 / bitmap operand; arg3: i32 / bitmap operand; arg4: i32 / bitmap operand; arg5: i32 / bitmap operand]. sub_479C70 pops parameter, mode, source, y, x, destination; handles must be < 0x4000, the mode one of 0-9, 0x20-0x27, 0x40, 0x41, 0x80, 0xC0, 0xC1, 0xF0, 0xFF and the parameter <= 0x100 (script errors otherwise). sub_402720 -> sub_40A530 clips and sub_40A9E0 dispatches the integer kernels (bitmap_blend.rs): 0x20/0xC0 alias 1/5, 0x21-0x27 run 2-4/6-9 with 256-p; incompatible formats (sub_40A9A0) are a script error, unsupported format pairs leave the destination unchanged. The 16-bit format-0 kernels are not ported; no script creates format-0 bitmaps.
//! `0x90:0x19` `Graph90_19_SynthesizeBitmap`: inputs=7, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[arg0: i32 / bitmap operand; arg1: i32 / bitmap operand; arg2: i32 / bitmap operand; arg3: i32 / bitmap operand; arg4: i32 / bitmap operand; arg5: i32 / bitmap operand; arg6: i32 / bitmap operand]. Target performs a three-resource bitmap synthesis.
//! `0x90:0x1A` `Graph90_1A_CompositeBitmaps`: inputs=6, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[arg0: i32 / bitmap operand; arg1: i32 / bitmap operand; arg2: i32 / bitmap operand; arg3: i32 / bitmap operand; arg4: i32 / bitmap operand; arg5: i32 / bitmap operand]. Target performs a six-argument multi-source composite.
//! `0x90:0x1B` `Graph90_1B_CopyBitmap`: inputs=4, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[arg0: i32 / bitmap operand; arg1: i32 / bitmap operand; arg2: i32 / bitmap operand; arg3: i32 / bitmap operand]. Target performs a four-argument bitmap copy mode.
//! `0x90:0x1C` `Graph90_1C_ScaleBitmapRegion`: inputs=10, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[arg0: i32 / bitmap operand; arg1: i32 / bitmap operand; arg2: i32 / bitmap operand; arg3: i32 / bitmap operand; arg4: i32 / bitmap operand; arg5: i32 / bitmap operand; arg6: i32 / bitmap operand; arg7: i32 / bitmap operand; arg8: i32 / bitmap operand; arg9: i32 / bitmap operand]. Target performs a ten-argument scaled-region operation.
//! `0x90:0x1D` `Graph90_1D_TransformBitmap`: inputs=4, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[arg0: i32 / bitmap operand; arg1: i32 / bitmap operand; arg2: i32 / bitmap operand; arg3: i32 / bitmap operand]. Target performs a four-argument bitmap transform/copy.
//! `0x90:0x1E` `Graph90_1E_BlitBitmapRegion`: inputs=8, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[arg0: i32 / bitmap operand; arg1: i32 / bitmap operand; arg2: i32 / bitmap operand; arg3: i32 / bitmap operand; arg4: i32 / bitmap operand; arg5: i32 / bitmap operand; arg6: i32 / bitmap operand; arg7: i32 / bitmap operand]. Target performs an eight-argument rectangular bitmap operation.
//! `0x90:0x1F` `Graph90_1F_CreateBitmapRegion`: inputs=6, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: bitmap handle; source: bitmap handle; x: i32 pixels; y: i32 pixels; width: i32 pixels; height: i32 pixels]. sub_47A590/sub_4033A0 allocate detached destination storage with the requested dimensions and source format, then copy through sub_40A530 using offset (-x,-y), mode 128 and parameter 0.
//! `0x90:0x20` `Graph90_20_StartObjectControl`: inputs=6, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[input_descriptor: u16-compatible value 0..=65535; input_enabled: bool/i32; frame_rate: nonzero i32 sampling denominator; duration_ms: i32 milliseconds, exactly 0 normalized to 1 ms; target_transparency: u32 0..=256; object: valid CDspObj/display-object handle]. `sub_47A6A0 -> sub_491B40 -> sub_431D10` keeps current X/Y, fixes update_numerator=0, validates input descriptor/transparency, rejects frame_rate=0, and installs CProcCtrlDspObj. Completion is asynchronous and follows the CProcCtrlDspObj wait/skip/cancel contract rather than returning a synchronous value from the syscall wrapper. Target sub_431F00 advances this exact control from its cooperative CProcedure poll; it is not advanced by a renderer-wide frame tick.
//! `0x90:0x21` `Graph90_21_StartNodeControl`: inputs=9, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[object: display object handle; target_x: i32 pixels; target_y: i32 pixels; position_curve: curve selector; target_alpha: 0..=256; duration_ms: milliseconds; update_denominator: i32; input_enabled: boolean; input_descriptor: input descriptor]. Target ABI descriptor `GROUP_90[0x21]=0x8009`; selector dispatches to sub_47A890 -> sub_491B40 -> sub_431D50; this is the XY/curve CProcCtrlDspObj form. Runtime advancement occurs only when this installed CProcedure instance is polled, matching sub_431F00.
//! `0x90:0x22` `Graph90_22_StartObjectControlEx`: inputs=7, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[object: display object handle; target_alpha: 0..=256; duration_ms: milliseconds; update_denominator: i32; update_numerator: i32; input_enabled: boolean; input_descriptor: input descriptor]. Target ABI descriptor `GROUP_90[0x22]=0x8007`; selector dispatches to sub_47A790 -> sub_491B40 -> sub_431D10; this is the alpha-only CProcCtrlDspObj form. Runtime advancement occurs only when this installed CProcedure instance is polled, matching sub_431F00.
//! `0x90:0x23` `Graph90_23_StartNodeControlEx`: inputs=10, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[arg0: control argument; arg1: control argument; arg2: control argument; arg3: control argument; arg4: control argument; arg5: control argument; arg6: control argument; arg7: control argument; arg8: control argument; arg9: control argument]. Extended alternate CProcCtrlDspObj constructor path.
//! `0x90:0x24` `Graph90_24_StartSpecialObjectControl`: inputs=12, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[arg0: control argument; arg1: control argument; arg2: control argument; arg3: control argument; arg4: control argument; arg5: control argument; arg6: control argument; arg7: control argument; arg8: control argument; arg9: control argument; arg10: control argument; arg11: control argument]. Target installs the special display-object control procedure through sub_491C40; its updater is advanced by that exact cooperative CProcedure poll rather than by the GUI frame callback.
//! `0x90:0x28` `Graph90_28_StartObjectMotionControl`: inputs=12, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[arg0: control argument; arg1: control argument; arg2: control argument; arg3: control argument; arg4: control argument; arg5: control argument; arg6: control argument; arg7: control argument; arg8: control argument; arg9: control argument; arg10: control argument; arg11: control argument]. Target installs the motion-control CProcCtrlDspObj path through sub_491D60; its updater is advanced by that exact cooperative CProcedure poll rather than by the GUI frame callback.
//! `0x90:0x29` `Graph90_29_StartSplineObjectControl`: inputs=12, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[object: CDspObj handle; point_count: i32 > 0; points: BP pointer to 16-byte XYZ+metadata records; position_curve: curve id; target_alpha: 0..=256 transparency; packed_alpha_curve_scale: low16 curve/high16 time scale (0 scale means 0x10000); fixed_parameter_target: i32, negative preserves start; duration_ms: milliseconds, zero normalizes to 1; update_denominator: catch-up denominator; update_numerator: catch-up numerator/enable; input_enabled: boolean; input_descriptor: packed input scope]. Target installs CProcCtrlDspObjBC through sub_491E60. sub_432490 builds three natural CSpline axes from the captured current fixed vector plus script points. sub_4325E0 is invoked by the exact cooperative CProcedure poll and samples CDspObj vtable+0x1C before and after applying fixed XYZ (+60), alpha (+72), and fixed parameter (+80); when the unsigned manager key changes it calls sub_443300 -> sub_4307D0 to remove/reinsert the object in CObjectManager, so moving fixed Z can change equal-priority GUI composition order during the animation.
//! `0x90:0x2C` `Graph90_2C_StartShakeObjectControl`: inputs=9, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[arg0: control argument; arg1: control argument; arg2: control argument; arg3: control argument; arg4: control argument; arg5: control argument; arg6: control argument; arg7: control argument; arg8: control argument]. Target installs CProcShakeDspObj through sub_491F90/sub_43C7A0; this selector is an object shake control, not a spline control. Its updater is advanced by that exact cooperative CProcedure poll rather than by the GUI frame callback.
//! `0x90:0x30` `Graph90_30_SetObjectDrawEnabled`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[object: display object handle; enabled: boolean]. Target vtable+4 writes CDspObj+0x14 and propagates the independent draw gate through children.
//! `0x90:0x31` `Graph90_31_SetObjectEnabled`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[object: display object handle; enabled: boolean]. Target writes CDspObj+0x04 and updates the inherited enabled gate.
//! `0x90:0x32` `Graph90_32_SetObjectAlpha`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[object: graph/display object handle; alpha_parameter: i32 transparency in 1/256 units]. Target sub_497DB0 rejects the alpha parameter as unsigned when it exceeds 256. sub_443460 requires a registered CDspObj, invokes vtable+0x48 to store the unconverted value at +0xAC and propagate it through the child chain, then requests an update when needed.
//! `0x90:0x33` `Graph90_33_SetObjectPosition`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[object: display object handle; x: i32 coordinate; y: i32 coordinate]. Target dispatches through vtable+44. Base sub_41B1B0/+40 writes CDspObj+0x30/+0x34 and recursively adds child-link offsets; several Back subclasses and Landscape override the slot.
//! `0x90:0x34` `Graph90_34_SetObjectMaskAlpha`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[object: display object handle; mask_alpha: i32 transparency]. Target sub_41B660 writes CDspObj+0xB0 and propagates the mask-alpha value.
//! `0x90:0x35` `Graph90_35_SetObjectFixedParameter`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[object: display object handle; value: i32]. Target invokes vtable+80 in mode zero and stores value<<16 at CDspObj+0xB8; it is not scale_x. For selector-1/internal raw writes used by CProcCtrlDspObj, sub_41B6F0 stores the 8.24 value verbatim. CDspObjSprite::SetFixedParameter sub_428470 always rebuilds mode-5 geometry through sub_4299A0 -> sub_4296C0 -> sub_429220 -> sub_429AF0 (and the corresponding mode-6 path); secondary-parameter value 3 only controls transition mirroring and is not a geometry-refresh gate.
//! `0x90:0x36` `Graph90_36_SetObjectSecondaryOffset`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[object: display object handle; x: i32 coordinate; y: i32 coordinate]. Target sub_41B320 writes CDspObj+0x40/+0x44 and propagates the secondary offset.
//! `0x90:0x37` `Graph90_37_SetObjectPrimaryOffset`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[object: display object handle; x: i32 coordinate; y: i32 coordinate]. Target vtable+56 writes CDspObj+0x38/+0x3C and propagates the primary offset.
//! `0x90:0x38` `Graph90_38_SetObjectProperty`: inputs=4, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[object: display object handle; property: i32 selector; value: i32; extra: i32]. Target forwards the four source-order arguments to sub_4438B0 and maps object/property errors. Generic CDspObj selector 196 (`0xC4`) reaches sub_41ADF0 and writes +0x48, gating Graph91:06 global display offsets. Selector `0x8000` reaches sub_41BEB0 and writes +0x80=`value`, +0x84=`extra`; when +0x80 is nonzero, the fixed-position setter rounds X/Y to whole 16.16 pixels when Z==0 or +0x84==1. Selector `0x8100` reaches sub_41BF10 and writes signed +0x24, an additive component of the vtable+0x1C CObjectManager sort key. sub_4438B0 samples that key before/after the property virtual and calls sub_443300 -> sub_4307D0 to remove/reinsert the object when it changes.
//! `0x90:0x39` `Graph90_39_SetObjectAlphaMultiplier`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[object: display object handle; multiplier: i32 0..=256]. Target sub_41B6A0 writes CDspObj+0xB4 and propagates the alpha multiplier.
//! `0x90:0x3A` `Graph90_3A_SetObjectPriority`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[object: display object handle; priority: u16 render priority]. Target vtable+84 writes CDspObj+0x1C; the object manager reinserts the object when its packed depth changes.
//! `0x90:0x3C` `Graph90_3C_SetObjectHitMaskBitmap`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[object: display object handle; bitmap: bitmap handle or -1/-2]. Target builds or clears the CDspObj hit mask and reports distinct missing-object/missing-bitmap errors.
//! `0x90:0x3D` `Graph90_3D_HitTestObjectAtPointer`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[object: display object handle]. Target obtains object and pointer positions, converts to local coordinates, and invokes CDspObj vtable+100 with hit-mask testing enabled.
//! `0x90:0x3F` `Graph90_3F_InvokeUnsupportedObjectExtension`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[object: display object handle]. All CDspObj-derived vtables in this target route slot +108 to sub_41BE90 (0x80000001), which the public handler maps to its target error path.
//! `0x90:0x40` `Graph90_40_SetCurrentObjectBitmap`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[bitmap: bitmap handle]. Target sub_47B5D0 validates the bitmap and sub_462130 stores it in the current display object, not in the global primary-bitmap slot.
//! `0x90:0x41` `Graph90_41_ConfigureCurrentObjectDualBitmap`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[primary_bitmap: bitmap handle; secondary_bitmap: bitmap handle; alpha_parameter: i32 transparency parameter]. Target sub_47B630 forwards two bitmap handles and the transparency parameter to sub_462140 for the current display object.
//! `0x90:0x42` `Graph90_42_ConfigureCurrentObjectQuadBitmap`: inputs=6, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[bitmap_0: bitmap handle; bitmap_1: bitmap handle; bitmap_2: bitmap handle; bitmap_3: bitmap handle; x: i32 coordinate; y: i32 coordinate]. Target sub_47B6C0 configures four bitmap resources plus a coordinate pair on the current display object.
//! `0x90:0x43` `Graph90_43_ConfigureCurrentObjectSpriteMask`: inputs=9, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[primary_x: i32 source coordinate; primary_y: i32 source coordinate; primary_resource: bitmap handle; secondary_x: i32 source coordinate; secondary_y: i32 source coordinate; secondary_resource: bitmap handle or sentinel; mask_resource: format-3 bitmap handle or -1; mask_parameter: i32 mask selector; alpha_parameter: i32 transparency DWORD]. Target sub_47B7C0 reverse-pops nine VM values; sub_462170 restores their natural source order into sub_43D750. CDspObjBackF construction installs blend selector 1; configuration stores two coordinate/resource pairs, accepts 0x7000/0x7001/0x7fff/-1 only for the secondary resource, validates an optional format-3 mask, then calls raw sub_41B620 to store the transparency DWORD. The selector-1 compositor is format-sensitive: format 1/1 reaches sub_40B4B0 while mixed/format-2 pairs use sub_40B5D0/sub_40B6F0/sub_40B9B0; the implementation therefore remains Partial.
//! `0x90:0x44` `Graph90_44_ConfigureCurrentObjectFrameTable`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[frame_count: i32 2..=32; frame_table: BP pointer to resource handles; alpha_parameter: i32 transparency parameter]. Target sub_47B930 copies 2..32 resource handles from VM memory into the current object frame table and applies transparency.
//! `0x90:0x45` `Graph90_45_ConfigureCurrentObjectResourceTriplet`: inputs=5, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[resource_0: resource handle; resource_1: resource handle; resource_2: resource handle; alpha_parameter: i32 transparency parameter; extra_parameter: i32 target field]. Target sub_47BA80/sub_4621B0 configures a resource triplet, transparency, and one extension field on the current display object.
//! `0x90:0x46` `Graph90_46_ConfigureCurrentObjectBitmapMode`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[bitmap: bitmap handle; mode: i32 0..=1; alpha_parameter: i32 transparency parameter]. Target sub_47BBE0/sub_4621D0 validates a bitmap, a two-value mode, and transparency.
//! `0x90:0x47` `Graph90_47_ConfigureCurrentObjectVmEffect`: inputs=5, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[bitmap: bitmap handle; auxiliary_resource: resource handle; record_count: positive i32; record_pointer: BP pointer; alpha_parameter: i32 transparency parameter]. Target sub_47BCC0/sub_4621E0 binds a bitmap and auxiliary resource to a nonempty VM record table and stores transparency.
//! `0x90:0x48` `Graph90_48_ConfigureCurrentObjectBitmapSizePosition`: inputs=5, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[bitmap: bitmap handle; x: i32 coordinate; y: i32 coordinate; width: i32 >= 2; height: i32 >= 2]. Target sub_47BE20/sub_462200 validates the bitmap and minimum dimensions and stores size plus position.
//! `0x90:0x49` `Graph90_49_ConfigureCurrentObjectBitmapSize`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[bitmap: bitmap handle; width: nonzero i32; height: nonzero i32]. Target sub_47BEF0/sub_462220 binds a bitmap and a nonzero width/height pair to the current object.
//! `0x90:0x4A` `Graph90_4A_ConfigureCurrentObjectBlitSources`: inputs=5, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[primary_resource: resource handle; secondary_resource: resource handle or target sentinel; mode: i32 required zero; alpha_parameter: i32 transparency parameter; flag: i32 0..=1]. Target sub_47BF90/sub_462230 configures two resources; the mode must be zero and the final flag is boolean-like.
//! `0x90:0x4C` `Graph90_4C_SetCurrentObjectRenderControls`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[draw_enabled: boolean-like i32; render_control: i32 target control]. Target sub_47C090/sub_462330 updates two current-object render controls and invalidates the object.
//! `0x90:0x4D` `Graph90_4D_GetCurrentObjectMode`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[none]. Target sub_47C0C0/sub_462340 returns the current display object mode field at +0x134; it is not a render-target handle.
//! `0x90:0x50` `Graph90_50_CreateSpriteObject`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[none]. Target sub_462350 allocates one of 512 CDspObjSprite slots and encodes the reusable slot as 0x80000000 | index. The manager create path sub_43E510 separately increments a monotonic Sprite construction counter and passes its previous value in ECX to sub_4256C0 -> CDspObj::CDspObj, producing CDspObj+0x18 sort_class=2 and +0x20 sort_index=construction counter; +0x20 is therefore not the public slot and is not reused after release/recreate.
//! `0x90:0x51` `Graph90_51_ReleaseSpriteObject`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[sprite: 0x80000000-tagged sprite handle]. Target rejects sprites still owned by active control procedures before releasing the CDspObjSprite slot.
//! `0x90:0x53` `Graph90_53_RefreshSpriteObject`: inputs=5, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[sprite: sprite handle; reserved_1: i32 ignored by target core; reserved_2: i32 ignored by target core; reserved_3: i32 ignored by target core; reserved_4: i32 ignored by target core]. Target sub_47C170/sub_462550 rebuilds/refreshes an existing sprite object. The public ABI consumes four additional values, but the target core ignores them.
//! `0x90:0x54` `Graph90_54_SetSpriteDrawEnabled`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[sprite: sprite handle; enabled: boolean-like i32]. Target 0x47C1F0 -> sub_462540 -> sub_43EE70 resolves a CDspObjSprite and invokes vtable+0x04. Base sub_41AE00 stores CDspObj+0x14 and propagates the draw-enabled value to native members. This is the same draw gate as generic 0x90:30 and CDspObjKnob 0x90:D4 forwarding; it is distinct from 0x90:31's CDspObj enabled field.
//! `0x90:0x55` `Graph90_55_SetSpriteAuxBitmap`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[sprite: sprite handle; bitmap: format-2/3 bitmap handle or -1]. Target sub_47C230/sub_462520 installs or clears the sprite auxiliary bitmap and validates descriptor format.
//! `0x90:0x56` `Graph90_56_ConfigureSpriteSingleBitmap`: inputs=7, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[sprite: sprite handle; x: i32 coordinate; y: i32 coordinate; bitmap: bitmap handle; blend_mode: i32 blend selector; alpha_parameter: i32 transparency parameter; priority: u16 render priority]. Target sub_47C2D0/sub_462370 -> sub_43E690/sub_426F50 configures sprite mode 0 with one bitmap and common display state. sub_427410 resets Sprite+0x244 to -1 before the subsequent virtual SetAlpha call, so alpha_parameter is applied to base CDspObj transparency even when the Sprite previously used mode 1. Title calls such as `(sprite,898,488,bitmap,1,256,1946)` therefore leave the image fully transparent at configuration completion; a later control performs the fade-in rather than exposing one opaque frame first.
//! `0x90:0x57` `Graph90_57_ReplaceSpritePrimaryBitmap`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=TargetMatched; params=[sprite: sprite handle; primary_bitmap: bitmap handle]. Current Tayutama2_trial_TG.exe sub_47C3E0/sub_462510 resolves the existing Sprite, then sub_43ECA0/sub_4272F0 replaces the primary bitmap and rebuilds mode-specific geometry for modes 0/2/5/6. Modes 5/6 clear the optional secondary transition source on this replacement path while preserving their projection/quad parameters. This is a Sprite mutation, not an offscreen-render operation.
//! `0x90:0x58` `Graph90_58_ConfigureSpriteDualBitmap`: inputs=9, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[sprite: sprite handle; x: i32 coordinate; y: i32 coordinate; primary_bitmap: bitmap handle; secondary_bitmap: bitmap handle; transition_value: i32 target transition field; alpha_parameter: i32 transparency parameter; priority: u16 render priority; transition_mode: i32 target selector]. Target sub_47C470/sub_462390 configures an existing CDspObjSprite as mode 1. It does not allocate a generic transition node.
//! `0x90:0x59` `Graph90_59_ConfigureSpriteScaledBitmap`: inputs=13, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[sprite: sprite handle; x: ordinary pixel anchor X; y: ordinary pixel anchor Y; bitmap: bitmap handle; transform_x: pixel transform term converted to 16.16; transform_y: pixel transform term converted to 16.16; rotation_16_16: signed 16.16 degrees; scale_x_16_16: signed 16.16 stretch ratio; scale_y_16_16: signed 16.16 stretch ratio; raster_mode_flag: affine blit selector stored at Sprite+0x280; blend_mode: i32 blend selector; alpha_parameter: i32 transparency parameter; priority: u16 render priority]. Current target sub_47C5D0/sub_4623C0 -> sub_427000/sub_4275B0 configures an affine-transformed full bitmap. sub_4291E0/sub_429220 compute transformed raster bounds/origin and sub_4281E0 draws at ordinary composite position minus that origin; these arguments are not source/destination rectangles.
//! `0x90:0x5A` `Graph90_5A_ConfigureSpriteMaskedBitmap`: inputs=10, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[sprite: sprite handle; x: i32 coordinate; y: i32 coordinate; bitmap: bitmap handle; mask_resource: format-3 resource handle; mask_parameter: i32 target field; fixed_parameter: i32 converted to 16.16; blend_mode: i32 blend selector; alpha_parameter: i32 transparency parameter; priority: u16 render priority]. Target sub_47C770/sub_462400 configures sprite mode 3 with a masked bitmap and fixed-point parameter.
//! `0x90:0x5B` `Graph90_5B_ConfigureSpriteVmEffect`: inputs=10, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[sprite: sprite handle; x: i32 coordinate; y: i32 coordinate; bitmap: bitmap handle; effect_resource: format-6 resource handle; record_count: positive i32; record_pointer: BP pointer; alpha_parameter: i32 transparency parameter; mask_alpha: i32 mask alpha; priority: u16 render priority]. Target sub_47C8F0/sub_462430 configures sprite mode 4 with a format-6 effect resource and nonempty VM record table.
//! `0x90:0x5C` `Graph90_5C_ConfigureSpriteTransformMode5`: inputs=17, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[sprite: sprite handle; x_16_16: signed 16.16 coordinate; y_16_16: signed 16.16 coordinate; z_16_16: signed 16.16 coordinate; primary_bitmap: bitmap handle; secondary_bitmap: bitmap handle or -1; transition_value: i32 0..=256; secondary_parameter: i32 target field; bitmap_origin_x: i32 source coordinate converted to 16.16; bitmap_origin_y: i32 source coordinate converted to 16.16; rotation_16_16: signed 16.16 degrees; perspective: positive i32 projection distance; project_position: bool i32; interpolation: bool i32; blend_mode: i32 blend selector; alpha_parameter: i32 transparency parameter; priority: u16 render priority]. Target sub_47CC10/sub_462460 configures mode 5. sub_429220 computes the inclusive transformed raster bbox, but case 5 of sub_4258D0 clips that bbox and sub_417730/sub_416750 inverse-map destination pixels into the source bitmap. Sprite+0x2A4/+0x2A8 fractional object position participates in the mapping. interpolation=0 selects sub_418280 nearest sampling; nonzero selects sub_417C50 bilinear sampling. The renderer must therefore preserve raster bounds separately from the affine source footprint rather than rotating/stretching the bbox as an ordinary quad.
//! `0x90:0x5D` `Graph90_5D_ConfigureSpriteTransformMode6`: inputs=20, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[sprite: sprite handle; x: i32 coordinate; y: i32 coordinate; position_parameter_3: i32 target position/transform field; primary_bitmap: bitmap handle; secondary_bitmap: bitmap handle or -1; transition_value: i32 0..=256; secondary_parameter: i32 target field; fixed_parameter_x: i32 converted to 16.16; fixed_parameter_y: i32 converted to 16.16; transform_parameter_0: i32 target transform field; transform_parameter_1: i32 target transform field; transform_parameter_2: i32 target transform field; transform_parameter_3: i32 target transform field; transform_parameter_4: i32 target transform field; transform_parameter_5: i32 target transform field; transform_parameter_6: i32 target transform field; blend_mode: i32 blend selector; alpha_parameter: i32 transparency parameter; priority: u16 render priority]. Target sub_47CF60/sub_4624B0 configures sprite mode 6 with three position/transform values, primary/optional secondary bitmaps, transition/fixed/transform fields, then blend, transparency, and priority.
//! `0x90:0x60` `Graph90_60_CreateFilterObject`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[none]. Target sub_462560 allocates one of eight CDspObjFilter slots and encodes the reusable slot as 0x90000000 | index. The concrete constructor uses CDspObj sort_class=7 and a separate per-registry monotonic construction counter for CDspObj+0x20, so release/recreate does not reuse the native sort index.
//! `0x90:0x61` `Graph90_61_ReleaseFilterObject`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[filter: 0x90000000-tagged filter handle]. Target sub_47D320/sub_462570 releases a CDspObjFilter. The prior GraphObjectUpdate interpretation was incorrect.
//! `0x90:0x64` `Graph90_64_SetFilterEnabled`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[filter: filter handle; enabled: boolean-like i32]. Target sub_47D350/sub_4625A0 writes the filter enabled gate.
//! `0x90:0x65` `Graph90_65_ConfigureFilter`: inputs=4, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[filter: filter handle; filter_parameter: i32 target filter selector; alpha_parameter: i32 transparency parameter; priority: u16 render priority]. Target sub_47D390 calls the full filter configurator with no mask, preserving filter parameter, transparency, and priority.
//! `0x90:0x66` `Graph90_66_ConfigureFilterWithMask`: inputs=7, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[filter: filter handle; reserved: i32 ignored by target core; filter_parameter: i32 target filter selector; mask_resource: format-3 resource handle or -1; mask_parameter: i32 target mask field; alpha_parameter: i32 transparency parameter; priority: u16 render priority]. Target sub_47D400/sub_462580 consumes one reserved ABI slot, then configures a filter with an optional format-3 mask whose dimensions must match.
//! `0x90:0x70` `Graph90_70_CreateMapObject`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[none]. Target sub_462680 allocates one of eight CDspObjMap slots and encodes the reusable slot as 0xA0000000 | index. sub_423920 constructs the object with CDspObj sort_class=1 and the manager supplies a separate per-registry monotonic construction counter for CDspObj+0x20; that native sort index is not the reusable handle slot.
//! `0x90:0x71` `Graph90_71_ReleaseMapObject`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[map: 0xA0000000-tagged map handle]. Target sub_47D6A0/sub_462690 releases a CDspObjMap slot.
//! `0x90:0x74` `Graph90_74_SetMapEnabled`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[map: map handle; enabled: boolean-like i32]. Target sub_47D6D0/sub_4626A0 writes the map enabled gate.
//! `0x90:0x75` `Graph90_75_ConfigureMapObject`: inputs=7, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[map: map handle; x: i32 coordinate; y: i32 coordinate; resource: bitmap/resource handle; blend_mode: i32 blend selector; alpha_parameter: i32 transparency parameter; priority: u16 render priority]. Target sub_47D710/sub_4626B0 configures map resource, position, blend, transparency, and priority.
//! `0x90:0x76` `Graph90_76_InitializeMapGrid`: inputs=5, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[map: map handle; columns: i32 1..=256; rows: i32 1..=256; cell_width: positive i32; cell_height: positive i32]. Target sub_47D820/sub_4626D0 initializes a map grid; each count is at most 256 and total pixel size is bounded by 1024x768.
//! `0x90:0x78` `Graph90_78_UploadMapTileData`: inputs=4, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[map: map handle; width: i32 extent; height: i32 extent; tile_data: BP pointer to u16 entries]. Target sub_47D900/sub_4626F0 copies a u16 map-data rectangle from VM memory into the map object.
//! `0x90:0x79` `Graph90_79_SetMapViewport`: inputs=6, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[map: map handle; source_x: i32 coordinate; source_y: i32 coordinate; cell_offset_x: i32 offset; cell_offset_y: i32 offset; wrap: boolean-like i32]. Target sub_47D9A0/sub_462710 updates the map source viewport, cell offsets, and wrapping selector.
//! `0x90:0x7A` `Graph90_7A_ReplaceMapTileId`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[map: map handle; tile_id: u16 tile identifier]. Target sub_47DA70/sub_462730 scans the first grid; when an entry equals tile_id, it writes the bitwise complement of the current second-grid entry. Target assembly advances the second-grid cursor once per cell plus one extra step after a match.
//! `0x90:0x80` `Graph90_80_CreateWindowObject`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[width: i32 native width unit; height: i32 native height unit]. Target sub_47DAC0 -> sub_4405B0 constructs CDspObjWindow. Values below 32 are multiplied by 32; final dimensions are bounded to width<=1920 and height<=32768. sub_42AE20 uses CDspObj sort_class=3 and the window registry supplies a monotonic construction index at CDspObj+0x20, independent of the reusable 0xB0000000 handle slot.
//! `0x90:0x81` `Graph90_81_ReleaseWindowObject`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[window: 0xB0000000-tagged window handle]. Target sub_47DB60 checks CDspObjWindow cooperative-procedure and owner links before sub_462980 releases the tagged slot.
//! `0x90:0x82` `Graph90_82_SetWindowCompositionOrder`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[window: window handle; mode: i32 enum 0..=5]. Target sub_47DC10 -> sub_440D60 -> sub_42C870 writes one of six permutations of 0,1,2 to CDspObjWindow+0x3C0/+0x3C4/+0x3C8. These values order the three composition passes in sub_42CA30.
//! `0x90:0x83` `Graph90_83_RenderWindowToBitmap`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination_bitmap: bitmap handle; source_window: window handle]. Target sub_47DBC0 validates the destination bitmap and sub_440C80 renders the second BP argument CDspObjWindow into the first bitmap. This closes both handle roles from target code.
//! `0x90:0x84` `Graph90_84_SetWindowDrawEnabled`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[window: window handle; enabled: bool/i32]. Target sub_47DC90 -> sub_440A90 invokes the window draw-enable virtual setter and invalidates the object when the value changes.
//! `0x90:0x85` `Graph90_85_ConfigureWindowObject`: inputs=7, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[window: window handle; x: i32 coordinate; y: i32 coordinate; blend_mode: target blend selector; transparency: i32 0..=256; reserved_validated: i32 0..=256; priority: u16 render priority]. Target pop order is priority,reserved,transparency,blend,y,x,window. sub_42B360 sets position, blend, alpha/transparency and priority. The reserved 0..=256 value is validated by the public handler but not forwarded to the core.
//! `0x90:0x86` `Graph90_86_SetWindowBackgroundBitmap`: inputs=4, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[window: window handle; decoration_error_context: i32 diagnostic context; frame_error_context: i32 diagnostic context; source_bitmap: bitmap handle]. Target sub_47DD80 pops [back_bitmap, frame_error_context, decoration_error_context, window]. Only window and back_bitmap reach sub_42B2A0; the middle values are diagnostic context. Bitmap -1 clears the background backing.
//! `0x90:0x87` `Graph90_87_SetWindowIsolatedComposition`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[window: window handle; enabled: bool/i32]. Target sub_47DE50 -> sub_42B3A0 writes CDspObjWindow+956. sub_42CA30 uses it to precompose backing, frame and text/children into an isolated buffer.
//! `0x90:0x88` `Graph90_88_SetWindowValidRegion`: inputs=5, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[window: window handle; x: i32 coordinate; y: i32 coordinate; width: positive i32 extent; height: positive i32 extent]. Target sub_47DE90 builds the inclusive rectangle `(x,y,x+width-1,y+height-1)`; sub_42B900 validates and stores it at CDspObjWindow+0x1A0..+0x1AC. These four fields are Window valid/content coordinates, not bitmap source-viewport/crop fields. sub_42C2A0 returns the same rectangle, and compact DCIPIcon construction sub_447C10 adds its left/top to each compact item offset.
//! `0x90:0x89` `Graph90_89_GetWindowValidRegion`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[out_rect: BP pointer to four i32 values; window: window handle]. Target sub_47DF50 resolves the BP pointer then sub_440910/sub_42C2A0 copies CDspObjWindow+416..+428. The portable VM now performs the same four-DWORD BP write and success return.
//! `0x90:0x90` `Graph90_90_StartWindowMessageProcedure`: inputs=6, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[window: window handle; text: Shift-JIS message string; procedure_value: i32; completion_control: i32; end_wait_policy: i32; allow_high_bit_input: bool/i32]. Target sub_47DFA0 validates a CDspObjWindow and configured font, then sub_4911E0 installs CProcDspMsg and returns scheduler status 2. Constructor fields +0x30/+0x38/+0x3C are completion_control/end_wait_policy/allow_high_bit_input; +0x40 is forced to one by the wrapper.
//! `0x90:0x91` `Graph90_91_SetMessageInputScope`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[mode: i32 enum 0..=2; scope_value: u16-compatible i32]. Target 0x0047E040 pops scope_value then mode and calls sub_432D80. Mode 1 requires scope_value < 0x10000; modes 0 and 2 ignore it.
//! `0x90:0x92` `Graph90_92_SetMessageInputFilter`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[enabled: boolean i32]. Target 0x0047E0E0 writes dword_565BAC through sub_432DC0. CProcDspMsg vtable slot 4 bypasses its base host-notify call when nonzero.
//! `0x90:0x94` `Graph90_94_SetGlyphRevealDelay`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[delay_ms: i32 milliseconds]. Target helper 0x004334C0 (MessageConfig_SetGlyphDelay) configures the per-glyph delay. The portable text runtime implements the setting, but exact tick rounding remains under target comparison.
//! `0x90:0x95` `Graph90_95_SetTextRevealAnimation`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[steps: i32 count; step_delay_ms: i32 milliseconds]. Target helper 0x004334D0 (MessageConfig_SetRevealTiming) confirms reveal steps/delay semantics. Parameters are listed in BP push order; the native handler pops step_delay_ms first.
//! `0x90:0x96` `Graph90_96_SetTextSettleAnimation`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[steps: i32 count; step_delay_ms: i32 milliseconds]. Target helper 0x004334F0 (MessageConfig_SetSettleTiming) confirms post-reveal settle steps/delay semantics.
//! `0x90:0x97` `Graph90_97_SetTextAutoAdvance`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[enabled: bool/i32; delay_ms: i32 milliseconds]. Target helper 0x00433510 (MessageConfig_SetAutoCompletion) confirms enabled/delay semantics. Runtime traces show enabled=0 and delay_ms=273 for the testcase, so continued skipping must come from another path.
//! `0x90:0x98` `Graph90_98_ConfigureMessageCaretFrames`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[frame_count: i32 count; bitmap_table: BP pointer to bitmap handles]. Target sub_47E1D0 -> sub_433300 clears the old global caret array, copies each bitmap into a 24-byte frame record, and accepts -1 as an empty frame. The portable VM now copies and validates the BP bitmap table; target caret-frame raster composition remains partial.
//! `0x90:0x99` `Graph90_99_SetMessageCaretFrameDelay`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[delay_ms: i32 milliseconds]. Target sub_47E250 -> sub_433480 stores dword_50765C; CProcDspMsg caret animation consumes it on each frame transition.
//! `0x90:0x9A` `Graph90_9A_SetMessageCaretPosition`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[mode: i32 coordinate mode; x: i32 coordinate/offset; y: i32 coordinate/offset]. Target sub_47E270 -> sub_433490 stores mode/x/y in dword_565B84/88/8C. Mode 1 is absolute; other values add the offsets to the window's current message position.
//! `0x90:0x9B` `Graph90_9B_SetMessageStartDelay`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[enabled: bool/i32; delay_ms: i32 milliseconds]. Target sub_47E2B0 -> sub_4334B0 stores enabled/delay in dword_565B90/94. CProcDspMsg copies them to +0x44/+0x48 and blocks reveal until the deadline unless ordinary input overrides it.
//! `0x90:0x9C` `Graph90_9C_SetTextShadowEnabled`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[enabled: bool/i32]. Target sub_47E2E0 -> sub_433520 writes dword_507674, consumed by the message glyph shadow/effect path in sub_433A70.
//! `0x90:0x9D` `Graph90_9D_SetTextShadowParameters`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[x_percent: i32 0..=100; y_percent: i32 0..=100; concentration: i32 0..=256]. Target sub_47E300 -> sub_433530 stores two font-height percentage offsets and the concentration. Portable CPU/GPU text paths now resolve both offsets from font height and use (256-concentration)/256 alpha; target font raster pixels remain non-bit-exact.
//! `0x90:0x9E` `Graph90_9E_RegisterFullwidthGlyphStrip`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[bitmap: bitmap handle; character_count: i32 0..=255]. Target sub_47E3A0 -> sub_432F50 clears the fixed atlas for nonpositive count. Otherwise it splits a horizontal bitmap into equal cells and registers them at private codepoints 0xFF01 onward. This selector is not a bitmap-backing copy.
//! `0x90:0x9F` `Graph90_9F_SetMessageInputForcesCompletion`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[enabled: bool/i32]. Nonzero allows an ordinary message input to complete CProcDspMsg even while glyph reveal is still active. It does not globally reveal text and is independent of AUTO.
//! `0x90:0xA0` `Graph90_A0_StartItemSelection`: inputs=8, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[window: window handle; item_count: i32 1..=16; item_strings: BP pointer to string table; column_count: i32 1..=16; layout_mode: i32; text_style: i32; initial_selection: i32 index; cancel_enabled: bool/i32]. Target sub_47E480/sub_491470 validates item_count, initial_selection and column_count, copies the string table, configures CProcSelectItem, and returns scheduler status 2.
//! `0x90:0xA1` `Graph90_A1_DrawItemSelectionGrid`: inputs=6, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[window: window handle; item_count: i32 1..=16; item_strings: BP pointer to string table; column_count: i32 1..=16; layout_mode: i32; text_style: i32]. Target sub_47E5F0/sub_491590 copies and renders the item grid immediately; it does not install a procedure.
//! `0x90:0xA2` `Graph90_A2_StartItemSelectionEx`: inputs=14, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[window: window handle; item_count: i32 1..=16; item_strings: BP pointer to string table; column_count: i32 1..=16; layout_mode: i32; text_style: i32; initial_selection: i32 index; cancel_enabled: bool/i32; primary_bitmap: bitmap handle or -1; primary_offset_x: i32; primary_offset_y: i32; secondary_bitmap: bitmap handle or -1; secondary_offset_x: i32; secondary_offset_y: i32]. Target selects CProcSelectItemEx and configures two optional overlay bitmap slots.
//! `0x90:0xA3` `Graph90_A3_StartItemSelectionExBlink`: inputs=14, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[window: window handle; item_count: i32 1..=16; item_strings: BP pointer to string table; column_count: i32 1..=16; layout_mode: i32; text_style: i32; initial_selection: i32 index; cancel_enabled: bool/i32; primary_bitmap: bitmap handle or -1; primary_offset_x: i32; primary_offset_y: i32; secondary_bitmap: bitmap handle or -1; secondary_offset_x: i32; secondary_offset_y: i32]. Target selects CProcSelectItemExBlink; its class enforces the initial 20-tick blinking/interaction gate.
//! `0x90:0xA4` `Graph90_A4_SetItemSelectionHighlightStyles`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[style_a: i32 style/color; style_b: i32 style/color]. Target sub_43B5A0 stores the two globals alternated by the selected-item blink renderer.
//! `0x90:0xA5` `Graph90_A5_SetItemSelectionInputMask`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[input_mask: i32 bit mask]. Target sub_43B590 stores dword_50762C, returned by the CProcSelectItem input-mask helper.
//! `0x90:0xA6` `Graph90_A6_SetItemSelectionNavigationParameters`: inputs=4, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[alternate_key_mode: bool/i32; cursor_move_arg1: i32; cursor_move_arg2: i32; cursor_move_arg3: i32]. Target sub_43B5B0 stores four globals used by navigation-key selection and pointer centering.
//! `0x90:0xA7` `Graph90_A7_SetItemSelectionColumnLayout`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[window: window handle; layout: BP pointer to 16 i32 values or null]. Target sub_441080/sub_42C7A0 toggles the custom-layout gate and copies exactly sixteen DWORD column anchors.
//! `0x90:0xAF` `Graph90_AF_SetInteractiveProcedurePollGate`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[enabled: bool/i32]. Target writes the same value into two input-poll gates consumed by item/icon selection routines; it is not a Win32 foreground-window check.
//! `0x90:0xB0` `Graph90_B0_StartIconSelection`: inputs=7, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[window: window handle; icon_count: i32 1..=64; icon_records: BP pointer; input_table: optional BP pointer; input_mode: i32 0..=3; procedure_state: i32; extra_image_enabled: bool/i32]. Target sub_491870 constructs CProcSelectIcon and parses 16-byte icon records. The previous shake interpretation was disproved by the target constructor path.
//! `0x90:0xB1` `Graph90_B1_StartIconSelectionEx`: inputs=7, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[window: window handle; icon_count: i32 1..=64; icon_records: BP pointer; input_table: optional BP pointer; input_mode: i32 0..=3; procedure_state: i32; extra_image_enabled: bool/i32]. Target sub_4919A0 constructs CProcSelectIconEx and parses 64-byte extended icon records.
//! `0x90:0xB4` `Graph90_B4_DrawIconBatch`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[window: window handle; icon_count: i32 1..=64; records: BP pointer]. Target sub_491AD0/sub_43A710 redraws 16-byte icon records immediately.
//! `0x90:0xB5` `Graph90_B5_DrawExtendedIconBatch`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[window: window handle; icon_count: i32 1..=64; records: BP pointer]. Target projects each 64-byte extended record to a temporary 16-byte base record before using the same batch renderer.
//! `0x90:0xB6` `Graph90_B6_ApplyIconInputLayout`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[window: window handle; descriptor: BP descriptor pointer]. Target validates the window, copies a compact nested DCIPIcon descriptor, and applies it immediately. sub_447C10 obtains the Window valid rectangle with sub_42C2A0 and constructs every compact child Sprite at `(valid.left + item.x, valid.top + item.y)`; this resolved position must remain unchanged when hover/selected resources are swapped.
//! `0x90:0xB7` `Graph90_B7_ApplyIconInputLayoutEx`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[window: window handle; descriptor: BP descriptor pointer]. Target uses the extended 40-byte root, 64-byte groups and 196-byte item records. Unlike compact sub_447C10, extended constructor sub_44A900 uses each item x/y directly and does not add the Window valid-region origin. Item records remain part of the configured logical descriptor independently of whether their bitmap can produce a live CDspObjVirtual. For each resolvable item, sub_41AB10 sizes the Virtual from the configure-time bitmap descriptor rather than the extended record's w/h fields; sub_4495C0 hit-tests the Virtual's final vtable+0x24 rectangle directly and reports no item when no live Virtual contains the pointer.
//! `0x90:0xB8` `Graph90_B8_CreateIconInputProcessor`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[window: 0xB0000000-tagged window handle]. Target creates the base DCIPIcon native type and registers it in the dynamic handle registry.
//! `0x90:0xB9` `Graph90_B9_ReleaseIconInputProcessor`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[processor: DCIPIcon registry handle]. Target `sub_46C4F0` removes exactly that dynamic processor and runs the DCIPIcon destructor (`sub_447B10` for the base type), which calls `sub_44A050` and `sub_41AC40` to release that processor's own per-item child/Virtual array and window attachment. The child array is owned by the DCIPIcon object, not by the referenced Window: two processors may reference the same Window and must keep independent item sets, and releasing one processor must not remove the other's children. This destruction is real target behavior. Scheduler ordering must not be changed to hide the transient state: reverse evidence for LoadProgramEx-created CThreads shows that newly constructed threads first execute on the next scheduler pass; only explicit status-3 thread switches are immediate within the current pass.
//! `0x90:0xBA` `Graph90_BA_ConfigureIconInputProcessor`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[processor: base DCIPIcon registry handle; descriptor: BP compact descriptor pointer]. Compact layout is root=32 bytes, group=52 bytes, item=60 bytes. Compact items contain x/y and bitmap ids but no explicit width/height; sub_447C10 resolves the configure-time normal or selected bitmap and derives the child rectangle from its bitmap descriptor. Failure to materialize one child does not delete that logical item or renumber its siblings. Root +0x14 is copied to DCIPIcon+0x48 and suppresses physical action bits before mapping; root +0x18 is masked with 7 and copied to DCIPIcon+0x4C to select one of eight 24-entry action maps. `sub_4485A0 -> sub_448690` samples pointer/keyboard input through `sub_46DF00`. Pointer eligibility is first arbitrated by `sub_46D830` over the descending native registration list installed by `sub_46D660/sub_46D6E0`: a candidate is rejected when any higher-id registered Window/Virtual under the pointer owns the scope. `sub_46DB40` then destructively drains each native descriptor event count before the mapped action is dispatched. Consequently one physical mouse-left edge is not broadcast independently to every live DCIPIcon: a real live-item Virtual hit owns the edge ahead of an overlapping processor-level no-item callback, and an action-1 MouseDown owned by DCIPIcon must not be replayed to `CProcDspMsg` as a second message-advance edge. Group fields: +0x08 current item (-1 or valid; configure invalidates a disabled item), +0x0C selection enable, +0x10 pointer-selection enable, +0x14 held mouse-left action-1 reinjection (not fresh-click permission), +0x18 selection-exclusion key. Item resource ids: +0x0C normal, +0x10 per-group selected/current, +0x14 pointer-hover, +0x18 auxiliary; -1 means absent. Configure keeps a processor-owned 20-byte live-item table. For each resolvable bitmap, sub_42B5B0 creates the private Window visual and sub_42AC50 creates a CDspObjVirtual hit wrapper; sub_41AB10 sizes the Virtual from the bitmap descriptor width/height returned by sub_407F20, and sub_41AB40 attaches it to the Window at `(valid.left + item.x, valid.top + item.y)`. Pointer hit-testing in sub_4495C0 queries each Virtual's final vtable+0x24 screen rectangle. The descriptor has no compact w/h fields, renderer clipping is not an extra sub_4495C0 hit gate, and each DCIPIcon processor owns this table independently even when multiple processors reference the same Window. Pointer raw-hit/current live separately at DCIPIcon+0x80/+0x74 and must not rewrite the descriptor or BC activation state.
//! `0x90:0xBC` `Graph90_BC_GetIconInputState`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[output: writable BP pointer to 6 i32; processor: DCIPIcon registry handle]. sub_46CC00 -> sub_4484C0 writes `[running, group, item, action_state, local_x, local_y]`: running is DCIPIcon+0x30 (configure=1; base action completion can clear it); group/item/action are DCIPIcon+0x68/+0x6C/+0x70 and remain `[-1,-1,0]` for pure hover/current-selection changes; sub_44A6F0 derives local coordinates only for nonzero action state. Hover is +0x74/+0x80 and group current items are exposed by BD/BE instead.
//! `0x90:0xBD` `Graph90_BD_GetIconInputCurrentGroup`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[output: writable BP pointer to i32; processor: DCIPIcon registry handle]. sub_46CC20 -> sub_448520 writes DCIPIcon+0x3C: -1 for none or a valid descriptor group index.
//! `0x90:0xBE` `Graph90_BE_GetIconInputSelections`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[output: writable BP pointer for group_count i32; processor: DCIPIcon registry handle]. sub_46CC50 -> sub_448530 writes each 52-byte group+0x08 selected/current item index in group order; -1 means none. Pointer hover does not modify these values.
//! `0x90:0xBF` `Graph90_BF_PopIconInputEvent`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[output: writable BP pointer to exactly 3 i32 / 12 bytes; processor: live DCIPIcon/DCIPIconEx registry handle]. return=[1 valid handle, 0 invalid handle]. Record=`[event_code,payload,parameter]`; valid empty queue writes `[0,0,0]`. sub_47F000 -> sub_46CC70 -> sub_448560 copies one FIFO head then sub_44A220 deletes it; BF never hit-tests or advances input. Confirmed base events from sub_448690: `0x10000001` raw-hit change with group/item or -1/-1; `0x10000002` pointer-current change with packed `LOWORD=item|HIWORD=group` or -1 and parameter=1 iff compact item+0x14 hover bitmap exists; `0x10000003` current-group navigation; `0x10000004/05` current-item navigation/selection notifications. Pointer-driven 04 requires group+0x10. Base activation updates BC via sub_449FA0/sub_44A000 and does not synthesize 06/07. Extended sub_44C170/sub_44C230/sub_44B9E0 produce confirmed `0x10000006/07`; extended activation also passes sub_44C6F0, which rejects source group+0x3C bit 0x02 or item+0xC0 bit 0x20. Pop is destructive; repeated polls cannot recreate an old event.
//! `0x90:0xC0` `Graph90_C0_LoadBgBitmapResource`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[bitmap: bitmap handle; namespace: string; name: string]. sub_47F040 validates the bitmap slot and forwards both resource strings to sub_401EF0, which requires target BG format.
//! `0x90:0xC2` `Graph90_C2_FlipBitmap`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: bitmap handle; source: bitmap handle; direction: 0 horizontal / 1 vertical]. sub_405590 mirrors horizontally for direction 0 and vertically for direction 1.
//! `0x90:0xC3` `Graph90_C3_DownsampleBitmapHalf`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: bitmap handle; source: bitmap handle]. sub_405090 rejects dimensions below 2 and creates ceil(width/2) by ceil(height/2) output through sub_418FA0.
//! `0x90:0xC4` `Graph90_C4_ImportExternalImage`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: writable BP pointer; filename: filesystem string; pixel_mode: -1,1,2,3]. sub_46A300 uses GDI+ GdipCreateBitmapFromFile and writes a caller-owned descriptor; portable host decoding does not claim GDI+ layout equivalence.
//! `0x90:0xC5` `Graph90_C5_SaveBitmapToImageFile`: inputs=4, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[filename: filesystem string; format: 0..=4; quality: i32; bitmap: bitmap handle]. sub_46A600 maps format 0..4 to BMP/JPEG/GIF/TIFF/PNG and saves the selected current bitmap.
//! `0x90:0xC6` `Graph90_C6_RegisterBgResourceData`: inputs=4, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[namespace: string; name: string; data: readable BP pointer; size: i32 byte count]. sub_401CB0 validates BG bytes and sub_450380 copies them into a lower-cased two-key cache.
//! `0x90:0xC7` `Graph90_C7_LoadCachedBgBitmap`: inputs=4, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[bitmap: bitmap handle; namespace: string; name: string; consume_cached: bool/i32]. sub_401CE0 looks in the two-key cache, falls back to archive loading, decodes BG bytes and optionally consumes the cached entry.
//! `0x90:0xC8` `Graph90_C8_TransformBitmapGeneral`: inputs=18, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[arg0: i32; arg1: i32; arg2: i32; arg3: i32; arg4: i32; arg5: i32; arg6: i32; arg7: i32; arg8: i32; arg9: i32; arg10: i32; arg11: i32; arg12: i32; arg13: i32; arg14: i32; arg15: i32; arg16: i32; arg17: i32]. sub_404FE0 validates destination/source and forwards seventeen transform operands to sub_40F970; the first public pop is not forwarded.
//! `0x90:0xCA` `Graph90_CA_ScaleBitmapAspectFit`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: bitmap handle; source: bitmap handle]. sub_405120 preserves aspect ratio, centers the scaled source and leaves letterbox/pillarbox space.
//! `0x90:0xCC` `Graph90_CC_RegisterToneCurve`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[identifier: i32; control_points: optional BP pointer to 6 i32]. sub_405420 registers three validated control-point pairs as three 256-entry LUTs, or removes the id when the pointer is null.
//! `0x90:0xCD` `Graph90_CD_ApplyToneCurveEffect`: inputs=8, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: bitmap handle; source: bitmap handle; color_before: packed RGB; amount_before: mix level; tone_curve: tone-curve id; color_after: packed RGB; effect_mode: i32; amount_after: mix level]. sub_405450 validates both bitmaps, tone-curve id, pixel/effect modes and color-film/monochrome mix levels before applying sub_40A2A0.
//! `0x90:0xCE` `Graph90_CE_EncodeBitmapToBuffer`: inputs=5, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: optional writable BP pointer; size_out: writable BP pointer; bitmap: bitmap handle; format: 0 or 1; parameter: 0..=100 for format 1]. sub_4056F0 validates dimensions/format, encodes through one of two target codecs, writes byte count and optionally copies bytes to caller memory.
//! `0x90:0xD0` `Graph90_D0_CreateKnobObject`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[target: display-object handle]. sub_463400/sub_442100 resolve any valid target CDspObj and allocate one of 32 CDspObjKnob slots; the target need not be unparented and multiple Knobs may reference the same target. sub_420EC0 stores only a raw target pointer at Knob+0x134--it does not add the target to the Knob member list--then copies the target mask-alpha, transparency and priority, queries the target rectangle through vtable+0x20 and initializes the Knob range to that exact width/height through sub_421200, inherits the target raw vtable+0x30 position, initializes relative drag mode=1, and aligns the target through sub_421430. CDspObjKnob uses sort_class=10 while vtable+0x1C/sub_421090 delegates the live manager sort key to the target. Host mouse input follows sub_463780/sub_4637C0/sub_4639C0: MouseDown captures the topmost knob before generic mouse-left input, sub_4212A0 preserves the pointer-to-thumb offset, mouse movement updates logical position through sub_421300, and MouseRelease ends capture.
//! `0x90:0xD1` `Graph90_D1_ReleaseKnobObject`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[knob: 0xF0000000 tagged handle]. Removes watch/order records and releases the tagged CDspObjKnob slot.
//! `0x90:0xD4` `Graph90_D4_SetKnobEnabled`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[knob: knob handle; enabled: bool/i32]. sub_4422B0 reaches CDspObjKnob vtable+4/sub_4210E0: it changes the knob draw-enabled state and forwards the identical value to the controlled target display object. This is draw visibility, not the separate CDspObj enabled field.
//! `0x90:0xD5` `Graph90_D5_SetKnobBasePosition`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[knob: knob handle; x: i32; y: i32]. sub_442320 invokes Knob vtable+0x2C/sub_421110 -> sub_41B1B0, whose virtual +0x28 dispatch re-enters Knob sub_421120. The Knob base position is therefore updated and the controlled target is moved through the target's own position virtual to `base + current logical slider offset`; the target is not a member child.
//! `0x90:0xD6` `Graph90_D6_SetKnobPosition`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[knob: knob handle; x: i32; y: i32]. sub_421430 validates logical coordinates independently, applies the 16.16 precision/range mapping, reads the Knob raw base through vtable+0x30, and invokes the controlled target vtable+0x2C with `base + pixel_offset`. Programmatic positioning therefore must update the target's native display-object state/propagation, not only renderer layer x/y.
//! `0x90:0xD7` `Graph90_D7_GetKnobPosition`: inputs=1, outputs=2, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[knob: 0xF0000000 tagged handle]. sub_421500 returns CDspObjKnob+312/+316.
//! `0x90:0xD8` `Graph90_D8_SetKnobMovementPrecision`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[knob: knob handle; x: i32; y: i32]. sub_4211E0 rejects negative X/Y precision and stores +332/+336.
//! `0x90:0xD9` `Graph90_D9_SetKnobMovementRange`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[knob: knob handle; x: i32; y: i32]. sub_421200 requires a range at least as large as the controlled target and stores inclusive maxima.
//! `0x90:0xDA` `Graph90_DA_TakeKnobVerticalEvent`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[knob: 0xF0000000 tagged handle]. sub_442490 calls sub_421570 and clears all four one-shot event fields. sub_421520 (mouse-wheel adjustment) records `(dx=0, dy=+/-1)` on every watched-wheel step and sets event-kind nonzero only when sub_421430 rejects the movement at a range boundary; DA therefore returns the unconsumed vertical delta only at that boundary and otherwise returns 0.
//! `0x90:0xDB` `Graph90_DB_TakeChangedKnobHandle`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[none]. sub_463970 scans the ordered knob records, clears changed flags and returns the last flagged handle. Pointer-driven sub_421300 position changes mark the corresponding portable knob record changed; programmatic Graph90:D6 positioning does not synthesize a user-change notification.
//! `0x90:0xDC` `Graph90_DC_SetKnobRelativeMode`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[knob: knob handle; mode: i32]. sub_421290 stores the relative pointer-offset mode at CDspObjKnob+320.
//! `0x90:0xDD` `Graph90_DD_SwapKnobInputMode`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[mode: i32]. Reads dword_507204, stores the new value and returns the previous process-global mode.
//! `0x90:0xDE` `Graph90_DE_WatchKnobObject`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[knob: 0xF0000000 tagged handle]. sub_4638E0 resolves the knob, allocates a new watch node and prepends it to dword_565FD0 without deduplicating. On WM_MOUSEWHEEL, sub_463880/sub_463920 consume the wheel through the first watch node and call sub_421520 with -1 for positive wheel delta and +1 for negative delta.
//! `0x90:0xDF` `Graph90_DF_UnwatchKnobObject`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[knob: 0xF0000000 tagged handle]. sub_463890 removes only the first watch-list node whose resolved Knob pointer matches; duplicate registrations therefore require matching removals.
//! `0x90:0xE0` `Graph90_E0_CreateGroupObject`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[none]. sub_442560 allocates one of eight CDspObjGroup slots. sub_420DE0 uses CDspObj sort_class=9 (base manager-key generation clamps it to 7) and a separate monotonic Group construction index at CDspObj+0x20 rather than the reusable group handle slot.
//! `0x90:0xE1` `Graph90_E1_ReleaseGroupObject`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[group: 0xF1000000 tagged handle]. sub_442650 releases the tagged CDspObjGroup and its member records.
//! `0x90:0xE4` `Graph90_E4_SetGroupEnabled`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[group: group handle; enabled: bool/i32 draw-enable gate]. sub_4426A0 invokes group vtable+0x04; sub_41AE00 writes CDspObj+0x14 and recursively propagates the same draw-enable value to current members. This is distinct from the base +0x04 object-enabled field.
//! `0x90:0xE5` `Graph90_E5_ConfigureGroupObject`: inputs=4, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[group: group handle; x: i32; y: i32; alpha_parameter: i32 transparency parameter]. sub_442710 calls group vtable+0x2C SetPosition(x,y) and then vtable+0x48 SetAlpha(alpha_parameter); both base setters propagate through current member records. The fourth argument is not priority.
//! `0x90:0xE8` `Graph90_E8_AddObjectToGroup`: inputs=4, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[group: group handle; object: display-object handle; x: i32; y: i32]. sub_442780 rejects invalid/self/already-owned objects. sub_41AB40 records local offsets, obtains the parent's live composite position through vtable+0x30/sub_41B260, and invokes the child vtable+0x28 setter at parent+local coordinates with member propagation enabled.
//! `0x90:0xE9` `Graph90_E9_RemoveObjectFromGroup`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[group: group handle; object: display-object handle]. sub_4427F0 requires an existing membership and removes it through sub_41AC40.
//! `0x90:0xF0` `Graph90_F0_OpenDirectShowMovie`: inputs=5, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[movie_path: Shift-JIS path/resource; x: i32; y: i32; width: positive i32; height: positive i32]. sub_480160 validates positive width/height, verifies the path and calls sub_48F270. The public wrapper pops but does not use x/y.
//! `0x90:0xF1` `Graph90_F1_CloseDirectShowMovie`: inputs=0, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[none]. sub_480260 calls sub_48F0E0, stopping playback and releasing the complete process-global DirectShow graph.
//! `0x90:0xF2` `Graph90_F2_IsDirectShowMoviePlaying`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[none]. sub_48F690 returns one only while the current DirectShow position is below duration.
//! `0x90:0xF3` `Graph90_F3_SetDirectShowMovieVolume`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[volume: 0..=128]. sub_48F6F0 accepts 0..=128; zero maps to -10000 dB and nonzero values use the recovered logarithmic-compatible target formula.
//! `0x90:0xF4` `Graph90_F4_LoadBurikoMovieResource`: inputs=4, outputs=0, procedure=yes, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[handle_out: writable BP pointer to i32; metadata_out: writable BP pointer to five i32; archive: optional Shift-JIS archive/path; resource: Shift-JIS resource name]. DCProcLoadBurikoMV validates the 16-byte BF_Movie_______ magic. sub_405B50 writes a handle plus five header DWORDs through caller BP pointers.
//! `0x90:0xF5` `Graph90_F5_ReleaseBurikoMovieResource`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[movie: BF_Movie resource handle]. sub_405CD0 removes one intrusive-list node, repairs parent/child links and frees shared bytes only when no linked handles remain.
//! `0x90:0xF6` `Graph90_F6_DecodeBurikoMovieFrame`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: bitmap handle; movie: BF_Movie resource handle; frame_index: nonnegative frame index]. sub_405E00/sub_405F10 distinguish invalid resource (3), frame range (4), bitmap dimensions/format (5) and codec failure (6). Procedure installation is controlled by the target async decoder gate.
//! `0x90:0xF7` `Graph90_F7_AttachBurikoMovieResource`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[handle_out: writable BP pointer to i32; source: BF_Movie resource handle]. sub_406120 permits only one attached child, allocates a shared child node, links it to the source and writes the new handle through the first BP argument.
//! `0x90:0xF8` `Graph90_F8_ClearSpriteTargets`: inputs=0, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[none]. sub_496270 unregisters every target and resets the target-number counter to zero.
//! `0x90:0xFA` `Graph90_FA_RegisterSpriteTarget`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[sprite: 0x80000000 tagged Sprite handle]. sub_4962A0 prepends a 20-byte node, registers the Sprite input region and assigns the next monotonic target number. Duplicate Sprite registrations are allowed.
//! `0x90:0xFB` `Graph90_FB_UnregisterSpriteTarget`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[sprite: 0x80000000 tagged Sprite handle]. sub_496300 removes only the first matching Sprite registration and unregisters its input region.
//! `0x90:0xFC` `Graph90_FC_HitTestSpriteTargets`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[none]. sub_496350 scans newest registrations first and performs an inclusive cursor-versus-Sprite-rectangle test.
//! `0x90:0xFD` `Graph90_FD_GetSpriteTargetState`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[target_number: i32]. sub_496430 samples bit zero of the primary input query once per main-loop pass; sub_496400 retrieves it by target number.
//!
//! ## Graph extended group 0x91
//!
//! `0x91:0x03` `Graph91_03_CacheBinaryResource`: inputs=4, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[namespace: Shift-JIS string; name: Shift-JIS string; source: readable BP pointer; size: byte count]. sub_480680 calls sub_401ED0 then sub_439930 and copies the sized BP payload into the enabled two-key graph cache.
//! `0x91:0x06` `Graph91_06_SetGlobalDisplayOffset`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[x: i32; y: i32]. sub_4806D0 calls sub_461E40 then sub_442EC0 and stores the two process-global CDspObj offsets. These are not added to every rendered layer: sub_41C0E0 applies them to a CDspObj composite position only when that object's +0x48 gate is nonzero. CDspObj::CDspObj (sub_41A400) initializes this gate by calling sub_41ADF0(1); Graph90:38 property selector 196 can change it afterward.
//! `0x91:0x0B` `Graph91_0B_SetScriptBitmapContextBindingEnabled`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[enabled: i32 boolean]. sub_480700 calls sub_48D210 and stores the main-loop gate for binding the active screen bitmap around BP execution.
//! `0x91:0x0C` `Graph91_0C_SetGlyphCoverageMode`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[mode: 0 or 1]. sub_480720 calls sub_42DC40 and changes the target linear or sine glyph-coverage conversion mode only for values zero and one.
//! `0x91:0x0D` `Graph91_0D_SetFontPitchDetectionEnabled`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[enabled: i32 boolean]. sub_480750 calls sub_42DC30 and stores the GDI pitch and family auto-detection gate used by native font creation.
//! `0x91:0x0E` `Graph91_0E_RegisterNamedFontTransform`: inputs=5, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[name: Shift-JIS font name; scale_x: 0 or 16.16 in 1.0..=2.0; scale_y: 0 or 16.16 in 1.0..=2.0; offset_x: i32; offset_y: i32]. sub_480770 calls sub_461D90 and registers a named four-value font transform after scale and coordinate validation.
//! `0x91:0x0F` `Graph91_0F_ConfigureNativeFont`: inputs=6, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[font_number: native face index; size: 4..=200; width_percent: 25..=200; bold: i32; field_56: i32; field_60: i32]. sub_480860 validates the numbered face, size and width, includes bold in the cache key and writes target font-record offsets 0x38 and 0x3C.
//! `0x91:0x10` `Graph91_10_GenerateAffineDisplacementMap`: inputs=5, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[bitmap: format-4 bitmap; center_x: i32; center_y: i32; span_x: i32; span_y: i32]. sub_480970 writes signed one-sixteenth-pixel affine offsets into a format-4 bitmap.
//! `0x91:0x11` `Graph91_11_GenerateRandomDisplacementMap`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[bitmap: format-4 bitmap; amplitude: i32]. sub_480A80 fills both displacement components independently in the inclusive negative-amplitude through positive-amplitude range.
//! `0x91:0x12` `Graph91_12_GenerateRippleDisplacementMap`: inputs=6, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[bitmap: format-4 bitmap; center_x: i32; center_y: i32; period: nonzero i32; phase: i32; amplitude: i32]. sub_480B20 calls sub_404130 to build a radial cosine scalar field and sub_403F40 to derive signed squared-difference gradients.
//! `0x91:0x13` `Graph91_13_GeneratePerspectiveBendMap`: inputs=5, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[bitmap: format-4 bitmap; center_x: i32; center_y: i32; parameter: i32; radius_or_perspective: i32]. sub_480C30 calls sub_4042E0 and combines polar horizontal mapping with a perspective radial vertical coordinate.
//! `0x91:0x14` `Graph91_14_GenerateCurvatureDisplacementMap`: inputs=5, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[bitmap: format-4 bitmap; center_x: i32; center_y: i32; parameter: i32; radius_or_perspective: i32]. sub_480D00 calls sub_404530 and generates a bounded nonlinear curvature field inside the supplied nonzero radius.
//! `0x91:0x15` `Graph91_15_GenerateRadialLensDisplacementMap`: inputs=5, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[bitmap: format-4 bitmap; center_x: i32; center_y: i32; parameter: i32; radius_or_perspective: i32]. sub_480E10 builds a sine radial scalar field and passes divisor 0x40000000 divided by curvature to sub_403F40.
//! `0x91:0x16` `Graph91_16_GenerateSineDisplacementMap`: inputs=7, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[bitmap: format-4 bitmap; x_period: i32; x_phase: i32; x_amplitude: i32; y_period: i32; y_phase: i32; y_amplitude: i32]. sub_480F20 calls sub_404910 and generates separable row-driven X and column-driven Y sine displacements.
//! `0x91:0x17` `Graph91_17_GenerateRadialWarpDisplacementMap`: inputs=6, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[bitmap: format-4 bitmap; source_origin_x: i32; source_origin_y: i32; warp_center_x: i32; warp_center_y: i32; radius_bias: i32]. sub_481020 calls sub_404B00 and derives the warp radius from the distance between the two supplied points plus radius bias.
//! `0x91:0x18` `Graph91_18_CompositeBitmapRectAlpha`: inputs=11, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: bitmap handle; destination_x: i32; destination_y: i32; source: bitmap handle; source_x: i32; source_y: i32; mode_or_key: i32; width: nonzero i32; height: nonzero i32; alpha: 0..=256; source_alpha_gate: i32 boolean]. sub_481100 validates both bitmaps, dimensions and alpha before dispatching the format-dependent rectangle compositor rooted at sub_4168E0.
//! `0x91:0x19` `Graph91_19_CompositeBitmapRectConverted`: inputs=11, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: bitmap handle; destination_x: i32; destination_y: i32; source: bitmap handle; source_x: i32; source_y: i32; mode_or_key: i32; width: nonzero i32; height: nonzero i32; alpha: 0..=256; source_alpha_gate: i32 boolean]. sub_481280 exposes the same public rectangle ABI and dispatches the alternate conversion compositor rooted at sub_417730.
//! `0x91:0x1A` `Graph91_1A_ReplaceBitmapRgbPreserveAlpha`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: format-2 bitmap; source: format-2 bitmap; packed_rgb: 0x00RRGGBB]. sub_481400 calls sub_4188D0 and replaces every RGB triplet while preserving the corresponding source alpha byte.
//! `0x91:0x1B` `Graph91_1B_ConcentrateBitmap`: inputs=5, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: bitmap handle; source: bitmap handle; concentration_x: 0..=0x10000; concentration_y: 0..=0x10000; brightness_attenuation: 0..=256]. sub_4814A0 calls sub_418CE0 after validating both 16.16 concentration factors and the brightness attenuation.
//! `0x91:0x1C` `Graph91_1C_ScaleTrueColorBitmap`: inputs=5, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: bitmap handle; source: format-1 or format-2 bitmap; scale_x: 16.16; scale_y: 16.16; interpolation: i32 boolean]. sub_4815C0 accepts only target true-color formats and allocates each destination dimension as source dimension multiplied by 16.16 scale.
//! `0x91:0x1D` `Graph91_1D_ProcessBitmap`: inputs=5, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: bitmap handle; source: bitmap handle; process_type: 0..=5; parameter: i32; alpha: 0..=256]. sub_4816F0 calls sub_4199D0 and selects one of six target pixel-processing operations with a native alpha parameter.
//! `0x91:0x1E` `Graph91_1E_ApplyGrayscaleMask`: inputs=4, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[target: format-2 or format-3 bitmap; grayscale_source: format-3 bitmap; offset_y: i32; offset_x: i32]. sub_4817F0 clips the shifted format-3 source and dispatches target format-specific mask processors sub_415B30 or sub_4155A0.
//! `0x91:0x1F` `Graph91_1F_CloneBitmap`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: bitmap handle; source: bitmap handle]. sub_4818D0 calls sub_403450 and clones the complete source dimensions, format, metadata and backing pixels into the destination.
//! `0x91:0x31` `Graph91_31_SetObjectSuppressed`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[object: CDspObj handle; suppressed: i32 boolean]. sub_481960 reaches sub_41ADA0 and writes CDspObj+0x0C, which sub_41AE30 tests inversely before drawing.
//! `0x91:0x33` `Graph91_33_SetObjectFixedPosition`: inputs=4, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[object: CDspObj handle; x: signed 16.16; y: signed 16.16; z: signed 16.16]. sub_4819A0 invokes vtable slot +60. Base sub_41B370 first consults +0x80/+0x84: if +0x80!=0 and (z==0 or +0x84==1), X/Y become `(v+0x8000)&0xFFFF0000` with 32-bit wrapping. It stores X/Y/Z at +0x4C/+0x50/+0x54; when +0x7C!=0 it then mirrors arithmetic X>>16/Y>>16 through vtable+0x28. The CDspObj base constructor sets +0x7C=1 and +0x80/+0x84=0/0, while Sprite mode 5/6 constructors and CDspObjBackML explicitly clear +0x7C. Finally sub_41B370 eagerly propagates each child's old-base delta in fixed coordinates. sub_41B4C0 resolves one object by adding its three fixed-vector banks and does not walk parents.
//! `0x91:0x36` `Graph91_36_SetObjectSecondaryVector`: inputs=4, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[object: CDspObj handle; x: signed 16.16; y: signed 16.16; z: signed 16.16]. sub_4819F0 reaches sub_41B580, stores CDspObj fields 27..29 and reapplies the primary vector through vtable slot +68.
//! `0x91:0x37` `Graph91_37_SetObjectPrimaryVector`: inputs=4, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[object: CDspObj handle; x: signed 16.16; y: signed 16.16; z: signed 16.16]. sub_481A40 invokes vtable slot +68; the base implementation sub_41B520 stores fields 23..25 and propagates them to children.
