//! `0x91:0xBA` `Graph91_BA_ConfigureExtendedIconInputProcessor`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[input_object: extended icon-input handle; descriptor: readable BP pointer]. 0x00484F20 -> sub_46CB60/sub_44A900 validates the extended variant and parses root=40 bytes, group=64 bytes, item=196 bytes. Root +0x14 suppresses physical action bits before mapping, +0x18 selects action-map mode 0..7, and +0x20 nonzero disables pointer processing. Group: +0x0C current item, +0x14 selection enable, +0x18 pointer-selection enable, +0x1C held mouse-left action-1 reinjection (not fresh-click permission), +0x20 exclusion key, and +0x3C flags. Item visuals: +0x20 normal, +0x24 hover, +0x28 selected, +0x2C hover+selected, +0x30 auxiliary. Group +0x3C bit 0x02 and item +0xC0 bit 0x20 participate in sub_44C6F0's immediate-versus-release activation policy: when the predicate is false, sub_448690 stores the hit item in its pending field and activates it on MouseRelease if the pointer still resolves to that item; these bits are not a disabled-button gate. Each resolvable item gets a processor-owned CDspObjVirtual created by sub_42AC50 and attached to the owning Window at the extended item's x/y through sub_41AB40. Immediately before attachment, sub_41AB10 writes the Virtual width/height from the configure-time bitmap descriptor returned by sub_407F20; the 196-byte item's +0x10/+0x14 w/h fields belong to the private visual construction and are not the sub_4495C0 hit-rectangle size. CDspObjVirtual::vtable+0x24 (sub_41B160) returns `[final_x,final_y,final_x+bitmap_width-1,final_y+bitmap_height-1]`, and sub_4495C0 tests that rectangle directly without an additional renderer/window clip intersection. CDspObjVirtual::IsEnabled (sub_42AD30) delegates to its parent Window. Configuration preserves every logical item record, while bitmap resolution independently decides whether that item receives a live Virtual; a missing child must not delete or renumber the descriptor item. The live-item table belongs to the DCIPIconEx processor, not globally to the Window, so processors sharing one Window must never replace or release each other's children. Mouse-left delivery still passes through the global native pointer-registration arbitration in `sub_46D830`; an overlapping DCIPIconEx whose item does not hit must not receive `sub_44B9E0`'s `0x10000007/-1` callback from the same physical edge when another registered processor has the live Virtual hit.
//! `0x91:0xBB` `Graph91_BB_SetExtendedIconInputItemState`: inputs=4, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[input_object: extended icon-input handle; group_index: i32; item_index: i32; state: i32]. 0x00484F60 -> sub_46CCA0/sub_44B460 updates one configured extended item and refreshes its child display object when active.
